# RDFS Schema for Business: Sports Entertainment

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix ind: <http://datamodel.lakehouse.org/business/sports_entertainment#> .

# --- Root Business Class ---
ind:Business rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label 'Business' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Root class for all business entities' .

# --- Specific Business: Sports Entertainment ---
ind:SportsEntertainment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Business ;
    rdfs:label 'Sports Entertainment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Sports and Entertainment is a live experience industry operating professional leagues, broadcasting networks, athlete management, venue operations, concerts, and fan engagement platforms across global markets.' .

# --- Domain Classes ---
ind:Event rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core operational domain managing the full lifecycle of live sports and entertainment events — planning, scheduling, production logistics, competition governance, and game-day execution. Owns event identity, fixture calendars, match results, season structures, tournament brackets, and event lifecycle from announcement through post-event reconciliation. Serves as SSOT for all event-related master data across leagues, concerts, and live experiences.' .

ind:Venue rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Facility operations domain managing stadium, arena, and concert hall infrastructure including seating inventory, concessions, parking, HVAC systems, building management (BMS), safety compliance (OSHA, ADA), and event-day logistics. Owns venue master data, capacity configurations, accessibility features, and operational readiness for live event execution.' .

ind:Athlete rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Athlete' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Talent management domain owning athlete identity, contracts, performance statistics (WAR, ERA, QBR), health records, eligibility status, and career lifecycle. Manages player rosters, draft selections, trades, transfers, injury tracking, NIL agreements, agent relationships, and compliance with league regulations including anti-doping (WADA) and collective bargaining agreements (CBA). Critical for league operations and broadcast content.' .

ind:Fan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Primary customer-facing domain and SSOT for all fan identity, demographic, and relationship data. Manages fan profiles, CRM segmentation, loyalty programs, membership tiers, NPS tracking, engagement history, and consent/privacy preferences under GDPR and CCPA. Serves B2C individual fans, family accounts, season ticket holders, VIP members, and fan club memberships across all engagement channels.' .

ind:Ticketing rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticketing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Revenue-generating domain managing the end-to-end ticket commerce lifecycle — inventory allocation, GA/VIP/SRO pricing tiers, dynamic pricing models, season ticket packages, group sales, resale marketplace, digital ticket delivery, access control, and PCI-DSS compliant payment processing. Integrates with Ticketmaster/AXS and Archtics for venue seating inventory. SSOT for all ticket transactions and access entitlements.' .

ind:Broadcast rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Media rights and distribution domain managing broadcast schedules, regional sports networks (RSN), OTT/IPTV streaming platforms, PPV event packaging, content delivery networks (CDN), and rights agreements. Owns media asset metadata, live feed distribution, blackout rules, DRM policies, replay content, and multi-platform delivery including linear TV and DTC streaming services. Critical for revenue generation through media rights deals.' .

ind:Sponsorship rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Sponsorship' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Partnership and commercial domain managing B2B sponsor contracts, brand activations, advertising inventory, naming rights, and partnership fulfillment. Owns sponsor identity, deal terms, activation deliverables, performance metrics (CPM, GRP), ROI tracking, jersey sponsorships, venue naming rights, broadcast integrations, and digital platform partnerships. Manages the full sponsorship lifecycle from prospecting through renewal.' .

ind:Merchandise rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Merchandise' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Product sales and licensing domain managing official team apparel, memorabilia, SKU catalog, inventory, e-commerce transactions via Shopify Plus, POS transactions, and retail operations. Owns product master data, licensing agreements, royalty tracking, IP protection, brand compliance, and omnichannel sales across venue stores, online platforms, and third-party retailers.' .

ind:Content rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Content' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Digital asset management domain owning video highlights, photography, social media assets, user-generated content (UGC), audio, and editorial content managed through Dalet Galaxy DAM. Manages content production workflows, metadata tagging, rights clearance (DRM), and CDN distribution for OTT, digital platforms, and social channels. SSOT for all content asset identity and rights metadata.' .

ind:League rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'League' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Competition governance domain managing league structure, division hierarchies, team franchises, season calendars, standings, officiating (VAR/TMO), rule enforcement, disciplinary actions, and competitive integrity. Owns league identity, franchise agreements, draft rules, salary cap compliance, CBA compliance, and regulatory oversight across professional sports organizations (NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS, FIFA, IOC).' .

ind:Finance rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Finance' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Corporate financial domain owning general ledger, cost centers, budgets, EBITDA reporting, ARR tracking, financial planning and analysis (FP&A), and SOX-compliant financial controls via SAP S/4HANA FI/CO. Manages chart of accounts, revenue recognition, expense allocation, intercompany settlements, and SEC financial reporting for publicly traded entities. SSOT for all enterprise financial master data.' .

ind:Workforce rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Workforce' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Human capital management domain owning employee records, recruitment, payroll, benefits, talent development, and organizational structure via SAP SuccessFactors. Covers full-time staff, part-time event crew, broadcast crews, league officials, and seasonal workers. Manages OSHA safety compliance and CBA labor agreement obligations. SSOT for all workforce identity and HR data.' .

ind:Compliance rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Compliance' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Regulatory and governance domain managing WADA anti-doping programs, GDPR/CCPA data privacy obligations, PCI-DSS audit trails, ADA accessibility compliance, CAS arbitration case records, and legal case management. Owns regulatory filings, audit schedules, incident tracking, policy enforcement records, and eligibility certifications across all governing bodies.' .

ind:Platform rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Platform' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Digital infrastructure domain managing fan-facing mobile apps, web portals, API integrations, personalization engines (Adobe Experience Platform), CRM systems (Salesforce), and digital experience delivery. Owns platform configuration, user authentication, session management, feature entitlements, SLA monitoring, ARPU/LTV/CAC digital performance baselines, and omnichannel orchestration enabling fan engagement, ticketing, merchandise, and content consumption across digital touchpoints.' .

ind:Partner rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Partner' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Vendor and supplier relationship domain managing broadcast partners, venue service providers, merchandise suppliers, technology vendors, and third-party contractors. Owns partner identity, contract terms, service level agreements (SLA), performance tracking, and procurement workflows. Distinct from sponsorship (which is revenue-generating partnerships) — this domain manages operational vendor relationships and supply-side commercial agreements.' .

ind:Analytics rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Analytics' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Enterprise analytics and business intelligence domain managing fan behavior models, predictive performance analytics, audience measurement frameworks, data science pipelines, and KPI dashboards for executive decision-making across all Sports Entertainment business units.' .

ind:Gaming rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Gaming' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Sports wagering and fantasy sports domain managing betting market definitions, odds feeds, responsible gaming compliance, fantasy league structures, prop bet catalogs, and regulatory reporting for licensed gaming operations across jurisdictions.' .

ind:Security rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Security' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Event security and physical safety operations domain managing credentialing, access control zones, surveillance systems, crowd management protocols, emergency response plans, and law enforcement coordination for all Sports Entertainment venues and events.' .

ind:Legal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:SportsEntertainment ;
    rdfs:label 'Legal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Corporate legal affairs domain managing intellectual property portfolios, trademark registrations, litigation case management, contract templates, outside counsel relationships, insurance policies, and corporate governance documentation.' .

# --- Data Product Classes (Tables) ---
ind:Asset rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Asset' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core master entity representing every digital content asset managed in Dalet Galaxy DAM — video highlights, photography, audio clips, editorial articles, social media assets, and UGC. SSOT for all content asset identity, format metadata, file specifications, ingest status, lifecycle state, and tag associations across OTT, broadcast, and digital platforms. Serves as the central node connecting rights, production, distribution, and analytics workflows.' .

ind:AssetVersion rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Asset Version' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Tracks every versioned rendition of a content asset — proxy, mezzanine, broadcast-quality, social-cut, thumbnail — including codec, resolution, bitrate, file size, storage location, and transcoding status. Supports multi-format delivery across CDN, OTT, and broadcast channels.' .

ind:RightsClearance rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Clearance' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SSOT for all DRM and intellectual property rights management associated with content assets — encompassing rights holder identity, territory, platform, usage type (broadcast, OTT, social, PPV), clearance status, expiry date, licensing fees, restriction flags, DRM enforcement policies (encryption scheme, device restrictions, concurrent stream limits, geo-blocking, offline download rules, watermarking requirements), and rights conflict detection and resolution (conflict type, conflicting records, resolution status, resolution action, responsible rights manager). Single operational record governing what content can be distributed where, when, how it is technically protected, and what conflicts exist against those rights.' .

ind:ContentRightsWindow rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Content Rights Window' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines time-bounded distribution windows for content rights — specifying platform, territory, start/end datetime, exclusivity flag, blackout rules, and associated rights clearance. Enables scheduling of content availability across OTT, RSN, PPV, and social channels within contracted rights periods.' .

ind:ProductionOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Production Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing content production work orders within Dalet Galaxy — covering video highlight packages, editorial features (story angle, journalist assignment, word count targets), social cuts, broadcast segments, and commissioned editorial content. Tracks assignment, production stage, priority, deadline, assigned editor/producer, output specifications, delivery status, and editorial approval workflow. Supports both technical production (video editing, audio mixing) and editorial commissioning (articles, features, interviews) as order types.' .

ind:IngestJob rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Ingest Job' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record for each content ingest event into the DAM — capturing source system (OB truck, camera card, social feed, UGC upload), ingest timestamp, file manifest, quality check status, metadata extraction results, and destination storage path. Supports traceability from raw capture to DAM registration.' .

ind:PublishEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Publish Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each content publication or distribution event — capturing asset, target platform (OTT, social, CDN, broadcast), publish timestamp, distribution status, CDN endpoint, geo-restriction applied, and DRM packaging applied. Provides the audit trail for all content distribution activity.' .

ind:MetadataTag rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Metadata Tag' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for controlled vocabulary metadata tags applied to content assets — including sport, league, team, athlete, event, topic, mood, and content type taxonomies. Supports structured tagging for search, discovery, personalization, and rights filtering across the DAM and digital platforms.' .

ind:Collection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Collection' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master entity representing curated groupings of content assets — highlight reels, editorial playlists, photo galleries, branded content packages, and PPV event content bundles. Tracks collection type, member assets with sequence ordering, curation method (editorial vs. algorithmic), publish status, and associated rights window. Supports ordered playlists, highlight packages, and curated galleries for OTT and digital platform delivery.' .

ind:UgcSubmission rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Ugc Submission' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record for each piece of user-generated content submitted by fans — capturing submitter identity reference, submission channel (mobile app, social, web), content type, moderation status, rights consent flag, usage rights granted, and integration status into the DAM. Supports fan engagement and UGC-driven content programs.' .

ind:ContentLicense rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Content License' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all outbound content commercialization agreements — covering individual asset licenses, bulk syndication deals (ongoing content feeds to media partners), third-party media outlet arrangements, social platform partnerships, broadcast partner feeds, and commercial licensees. Captures licensee/partner identity, licensed scope (asset, collection, sport, league), deal type (one-off license, ongoing syndication, revenue-share partnership), territory, usage type, fee structure (flat fee, royalty, revenue share), delivery format and schedule, content feed frequency, start/end dates, auto-renewal terms, and compliance status. SSOT for all outbound content monetization distinct from inbound rights_clearance.' .

ind:ContentDrmPolicy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Content Drm Policy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference entity defining DRM enforcement policies applied during content packaging and distribution — specifying encryption scheme, playback device restrictions, offline download rules, concurrent stream limits, geo-blocking rules, and watermarking requirements. Applied at publish time to govern content protection across OTT and digital platforms.' .

ind:EditorialBrief rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Editorial Brief' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for editorial content briefs — capturing story angle, assigned journalist or producer, target platform, sport/league/event context, word count or duration target, deadline, approval workflow status, and associated production order. Governs the editorial content production pipeline from commissioning to publication.' .

ind:PlatformChannel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Platform Channel' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference master for all distribution platform channels — OTT apps, RSN broadcast slots, social media channels, DTC streaming, IPTV, and PPV portals. Captures platform name, channel type, operator, territory, supported content formats, and DRM requirements. Used to route publish events and rights windows to the correct distribution endpoint.' .

ind:RightsConflict rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Conflict' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing detected rights conflicts — where a scheduled publish event or distribution request violates an active rights window, territory restriction, or DRM policy. Captures conflict type, conflicting rights records, resolution status, resolution action taken, and responsible rights manager. Supports rights compliance governance.' .

ind:AssetUsage rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Asset Usage' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing each instance of content asset consumption or reuse — tracking which asset was used, in which production order, broadcast segment, social post, or sponsorship activation, usage type, usage date, and associated rights window. Provides the audit trail for rights compliance and royalty calculation.' .

ind:Approval rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Approval' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional workflow record tracking the editorial and legal approval lifecycle of content assets before publication — capturing approval stage, reviewer identity, approval decision, rejection reason, revision request notes, and approval timestamp. Supports multi-stage review workflows for broadcast, OTT, and social content.' .

ind:SyndicationDeal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Syndication Deal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for content syndication agreements with third-party media partners — capturing partner identity reference, syndicated content scope (sport, league, asset type), territory, syndication fee, revenue share terms, delivery format, delivery schedule, and contract period. Distinct from content_license in that syndication deals govern ongoing bulk content feeds rather than individual asset licenses.' .

ind:TicketInventory rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticket Inventory' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all available ticket inventory units within the venue seating manifest, sourced from Archtics/Ticketmaster Host. Tracks seat-level availability, hold status, kill status, accessibility designations (ADA), inventory pool assignments (GA, VIP, SRO, press, complimentary), and event-specific price zone mapping. SSOT for what seats exist per event and their current allocation state prior to sale. Supports real-time available-to-sell calculations across all channels.' .

ind:TicketOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticket Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core transactional record capturing a fan\'s purchase of one or more tickets through any sales channel (Ticketmaster, AXS, box office, group sales, DTC, kiosk, partner API). Records order status, sales channel code, purchase timestamp, total face value, fees, taxes, PCI-DSS compliant payment reference, cashier/agent ID (for box office), and delivery method. SSOT for all ticket commerce transactions regardless of channel. Supports multi-channel reconciliation and revenue attribution.' .

ind:TicketOrderLine rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticket Order Line' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Line-item detail within a ticket order representing a single ticket unit sold. Captures seat assignment, price tier, face value, service fee, facility fee, dynamic price applied, barcode/token, delivery method, delivery status, delivery timestamp, and comp flag with reason code. Enables per-seat revenue attribution, access control entitlement generation, fulfillment tracking, and complimentary ticket audit.' .

ind:PriceTier rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Price Tier' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference catalog of pricing tiers available for ticket inventory, including GA (General Admission), VIP, SRO (Standing Room Only), premium club, suite, and accessible seating tiers. Defines base face value, fee structures, and eligibility rules per tier. Used by dynamic pricing engine and order processing.' .

ind:DynamicPriceRule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Dynamic Price Rule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Business rules governing real-time dynamic pricing adjustments for ticket inventory. Captures demand signals, floor/ceiling price bounds, adjustment algorithms (demand-based, time-to-event, competitor benchmarking), activation windows, and event-specific overrides. Enables yield management across GA/VIP/SRO tiers.' .

ind:SeasonTicketPackage rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Season Ticket Package' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for season ticket packages offered to fans, including full-season, half-season, mini-plan, and flex-pack configurations. Tracks package type, included events, seat assignments, face value, renewal priority rights, and STH (Season Ticket Holder) benefits. SSOT for season ticket product definitions.' .

ind:SeasonTicketAccount rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Season Ticket Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record linking a fan account to an active season ticket package. Captures enrollment date, seat assignments, payment plan status, renewal status, account balance, STH loyalty tier, and communication preferences. Represents the active season ticket holder relationship and entitlement.' .

ind:GroupSale rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Group Sale' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record for group ticket sales involving 10+ tickets sold to a single organizational buyer (corporate outings, school field trips, community organizations, birthday parties, suite buyouts). Tracks group name, size, negotiated discount rate, group coordinator contact, deposit schedule, payment milestones, fulfillment status, assigned seating block, catering/hospitality add-ons, and group experience package. Managed as distinct workflow from individual retail sales with separate approval and pricing authority.' .

ind:Resale rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Resale' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified lifecycle record for all secondary market and peer-to-peer ticket activity. Captures listing creation (price, channel, seller type, listing status), marketplace transaction execution (sale price, platform fees, seller proceeds, buyer reference), and peer-to-peer transfers (gift, forward). Tracks movement type, transfer timestamp, new entitlement token issuance, transfer restrictions, anti-scalping rule compliance, and revenue share calculations. SSOT for all secondary market listings, resale transactions, and fan-to-fan ticket transfers. Replaces separate listing and transaction records with a single lifecycle entity progressing through states: listed → sold/transferred/expired/withdrawn.' .

ind:AccessEntitlement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Access Entitlement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Digital entitlement record granting a specific fan the right to access a venue for a specific event. Generated upon ticket purchase or transfer. Contains barcode/QR token, NFC credential, validity window, seat assignment, access zone, and current entitlement status (valid, used, voided, transferred). SSOT for access control decisions at gate.' .

ind:GateScan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Gate Scan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each access control scan event at venue entry points. Captures entitlement token scanned, gate/turnstile identifier, scan timestamp, scan result (granted, denied, duplicate), operator ID, and device ID. Feeds real-time attendance tracking and post-event access audit. Sourced from Ticketmaster/AXS access control hardware.' .

ind:TicketPayment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticket Payment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'PCI-DSS compliant payment transaction record associated with a ticket order. Captures payment method type, masked card/wallet reference, payment processor token, authorization code, amount charged, currency, payment status (authorized, captured, failed, refunded), and settlement reference. SSOT for ticketing payment financial records.' .

ind:Refund rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Refund' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of a ticket refund or credit issued to a fan. Captures originating order reference, refund reason (event cancellation, postponement, fan request, fraud), refund amount, refund method (original payment, credit wallet, voucher), processing status, and approval workflow state. Supports PCI-DSS refund audit requirements.' .

ind:HoldAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Hold Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of ticket inventory blocks placed on hold for specific purposes — sponsor complimentary holds, artist/athlete holds, media holds, ADA holds, operational holds, pre-sale windows (with access codes and eligibility criteria), and comp allocations. Captures hold type, quantity, seat block, hold owner, hold expiry, release status, presale time windows, and access eligibility rules. Manages inventory allocation before public on-sale and enables tiered on-sale sequencing.' .

ind:Sponsor rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Sponsor' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all sponsoring organizations and brands in the sports-entertainment ecosystem. Captures sponsor identity, corporate hierarchy, industry classification, account tier (title, presenting, official, associate), CRM account linkage from Salesforce, contact details, and relationship status. SSOT for sponsor identity across all commercial and activation workflows.' .

ind:Deal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Deal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core sponsorship deal record representing a negotiated commercial agreement between Sports Entertainment and a sponsor. Captures deal name, deal type (jersey sponsorship, venue naming rights, broadcast integration, digital platform partnership, presenting sponsor, official partner), total contract value (TCV), deal stage (prospecting, negotiation, executed, active, expired, renewed), start and end dates, exclusivity category and scope, territory. For naming rights deals: named asset (stadium, arena, practice facility, trophy, award, league division), signage specifications, broadcast mention requirements, digital property URL changes, and renewal option details. For digital partnerships: partnership type (app title sponsor, OTT streaming sponsor, social media co-branding, DTC campaign integration, API data partnership, Adobe Experience Platform personalization), digital property, impression commitment, CTR target, ARPU impact estimate, GDPR/CCPA data-sharing consent scope, and campaign flight dates. Includes originating Salesforce opportunity reference and renewal option flags. Central entity in the sponsorship lifecycle from prospecting through renewal, encompassing all deal sub-types.' .

ind:DealTerm rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Deal Term' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Detailed contractual terms and financial obligations associated with a sponsorship deal. Captures payment schedule type (annual, quarterly, milestone), total fee, cash vs. value-in-kind (VIK) split, escalation clauses, performance bonuses, kill-clause thresholds, renewal options, right-of-first-refusal flags, and governing law jurisdiction. Supports SAP S/4HANA SD billing integration for invoicing milestones.' .

ind:DealAmendment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Deal Amendment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Tracks formal amendments and modifications to executed sponsorship deals. Captures amendment number, amendment type (fee adjustment, term extension, asset swap, territory expansion, force majeure relief), effective date, reason code, approval status, approver identity, and delta values for changed financial terms. Maintains a complete audit trail of deal evolution over the sponsorship lifecycle.' .

ind:SponsorshipActivation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Sponsorship Activation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for individual brand activation deliverables committed within a sponsorship deal. Captures activation name, activation category (in-venue signage, jersey patch/sleeve/collar placement, broadcast billboard, virtual LED overlay, sponsored segment, branded replay, digital banner, social media post, experiential activation, naming rights display, PA announcement, LED perimeter board, halftime show integration, broadcast integration type with network/OTT platform association, airtime and duration), placement specifications (location, dimensions, visibility tier, kit manufacturer for jersey placements), scheduled and actual delivery dates, fulfillment status, responsible team, broadcast window, FCC/regulatory disclosure requirements, DRM compliance flags, and associated event. Core entity for tracking what was promised vs. delivered across all activation channels including broadcast integrations, jersey placements, and digital activations.' .

ind:ActivationFulfillment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Activation Fulfillment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing the actual execution and proof-of-performance for each brand activation. Records fulfillment date, fulfillment channel (broadcast, in-venue, digital, social, OTT), proof-of-play reference (screenshot, broadcast log timestamp, photo), impressions delivered, GRP achieved, CPM realized, fulfillment quality rating, and any shortfall notes. Feeds ROI reporting and renewal negotiations.' .

ind:NamingRight rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Naming Right' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for venue and property naming rights agreements. Captures named asset (stadium, arena, practice facility, trophy, award, league division), naming rights holder (sponsor), naming rights fee, term start and end dates, signage specifications, broadcast mention requirements, digital property URL changes, and renewal option details. Distinct from general deal terms due to the long-term, high-value, and multi-property nature of naming rights.' .

ind:JerseySponsorship rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Jersey Sponsorship' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for jersey and kit sponsorship placements. Captures placement location (front chest, sleeve, back collar, shorts, training kit), sponsor brand, team or athlete association, kit manufacturer, placement dimensions, broadcast visibility tier, exclusivity scope, and term dates. Tracks both primary jersey sponsors and secondary placement sponsors across all league teams and individual athletes under NIL arrangements.' .

ind:SponsorshipAdInventory rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Sponsorship Ad Inventory' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of available sponsorship and advertising inventory assets across all Sports Entertainment properties, including independently assessed market valuations. Captures asset type (LED perimeter board, broadcast billboard, digital overlay, PA announcement slot, in-app banner, OTT pre-roll, social media post, VIP hospitality suite, naming rights unit), property association (venue, broadcast channel, OTT platform, mobile app), capacity metrics (number of units, duration in seconds, estimated impressions), exclusivity category, current availability status. Includes valuation data: assessed value per unit, valuation methodology (broadcast equivalency, Nielsen media value, independent agency assessment), valuation date, valuation source, and currency. SSOT for what can be sold to sponsors, current market value of each asset, and benchmarking against industry CPM and GRP rates.' .

ind:InventoryAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Inventory Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record linking specific ad inventory units to sponsorship deals and activations. Captures allocation date, allocated quantity, event or broadcast window, exclusivity flag, priority tier, and allocation status (reserved, confirmed, delivered, cancelled). Prevents double-booking of inventory assets and supports capacity planning for future deal negotiations.' .

ind:BroadcastIntegration rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Integration' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for sponsor integrations within broadcast and OTT/IPTV productions. Captures integration type (virtual LED overlay, sponsored segment title card, branded replay, sponsored statistics graphic, PPV pre-show sponsor, RSN billboard), broadcast window, network or OTT platform, scheduled airtime, duration in seconds, DRM compliance flag, and FCC disclosure requirements. Bridges sponsorship commitments with the broadcast domain\'s production schedule.' .

ind:DigitalPartnership rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Digital Partnership' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for digital and platform-based sponsorship partnerships. Captures partnership type (app title sponsor, website banner, OTT streaming sponsor, social media co-branding, DTC campaign integration, API data partnership, Adobe Experience Platform personalization integration), digital property, impression commitment, click-through rate (CTR) target, ARPU impact estimate, GDPR/CCPA data-sharing consent scope, and campaign flight dates.' .

ind:PerformanceMetric rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Performance Metric' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing measured sponsorship performance data against contracted KPIs. Records metric type (GRP delivered, CPM realized, impressions, reach, frequency, brand recall score, NPS lift, social media engagement rate, broadcast airtime seconds, in-venue dwell time), measurement period, actual value, contracted target value, variance, measurement methodology, and data source (Nielsen, Kantar, internal analytics). Feeds ROI reporting and renewal negotiations.' .

ind:RoiReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Roi Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic sponsorship ROI valuation report produced for each sponsor summarizing the total media value, activation delivery rate, audience reach, brand exposure value, and financial return against contracted fees. Captures report period, total media value equivalent (MVE), total contracted value, ROI ratio, fulfillment rate percentage, key highlights, and report delivery date. Distinct from raw performance_metric records — this is the aggregated valuation document shared with sponsors during review meetings and renewal negotiations.' .

ind:PaymentSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Payment Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record defining the contractual payment milestones and installment schedule for a sponsorship deal. Captures milestone name, due date, payment amount, payment type (cash, VIK, barter), invoice reference, payment status (scheduled, invoiced, received, overdue), and SAP S/4HANA FI document number. Supports accounts receivable tracking and cash flow forecasting for the finance domain.' .

ind:HospitalityEntitlement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Hospitality Entitlement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for VIP hospitality benefits and entitlements included in sponsorship deals, with integrated line-item redemption tracking. Captures entitlement type (suite access, VIP tickets, field/pitch access passes, meet-and-greet packages, athlete appearance, executive box, travel and accommodation), quantity per event, event scope (all home games, playoffs, specific events), remaining balance. Includes redemption line items: redemption date, event, entitlement type redeemed, quantity used, sponsor contact who redeemed, redemption channel (online portal, account manager), and satisfaction rating. Supports sponsor relationship management, entitlement balance tracking, utilization reporting, and informs renewal package design.' .

ind:EntitlementRedemption rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Entitlement Redemption' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record capturing the actual use of VIP hospitality entitlements by sponsor representatives. Records redemption date, event, entitlement type redeemed, quantity used, sponsor contact who redeemed, redemption channel (online portal, account manager), and satisfaction rating. Enables entitlement balance tracking and informs renewal package design.' .

ind:Prospect rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Prospect' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for prospective sponsors in the pipeline before a deal is executed. Captures prospect organization name, industry vertical, estimated deal value, target sponsorship category, assigned account executive, pipeline stage (identified, qualified, pitched, proposal sent, negotiating), probability of close, expected close date, and Salesforce lead/opportunity reference. SSOT for the pre-deal commercial pipeline.' .

ind:Renewal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Renewal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record tracking the renewal lifecycle of expiring sponsorship deals. Captures renewal initiation date, renewal type (auto-renewal, renegotiated, multi-year extension), proposed new TCV, proposed term dates, renewal stage (initiated, under negotiation, agreed, declined, lapsed), key negotiation notes, and outcome. Enables proactive renewal management and retention rate tracking.' .

ind:AssetValuation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Asset Valuation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference and transactional record capturing the independently assessed market value of individual sponsorship inventory assets. Captures asset type, valuation methodology (broadcast equivalency, Nielsen media value, independent agency assessment), assessed value per unit, valuation date, valuation source, and currency. Used to price new deals, validate ROI claims, and benchmark against industry CPM and GRP rates.' .

ind:Fixture rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Fixture' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core master entity and SSOT for event identity — any scheduled live sports or entertainment event. Captures event name, type (match, concert, PPV, exhibition, all-star, draft, awards), status (announced → confirmed → in-progress → completed/cancelled), scheduled date/time with timezone, doors-open time, event tier (regular season, playoff, championship, special event), home/away designation, neutral site flag, broadcast eligibility flag, classification (league, cup, friendly, touring), and lifecycle timestamps. Anchor entity referenced by all downstream domains.' .

ind:Calendar rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Calendar' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master entity defining a competitive or programming season within a league or entertainment series. Serves as the SSOT for season identity AND the official published fixture calendar/schedule. Captures season name, year, sport/entertainment type, start/end dates, number of scheduled rounds/weeks, playoff structure flag, season status (planning, active, completed), governing body reference, CBA applicability flag, season format (regular, shortened, expanded), calendar publication date, calendar version, scheduling authority, blackout dates, bye weeks, international window dates, and calendar status (draft, published, amended). Owns the official release of fixture schedules to downstream consumers including broadcast, ticketing, and venue operations.' .

ind:Tournament rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Tournament' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master entity representing a structured competition format — knockout brackets, round-robin groups, double elimination, or multi-stage tournaments (e.g., FIFA World Cup, NBA Playoffs, UFC Championship Series). Captures tournament name, format type, number of rounds, seeding methodology, host region, prize pool amount, governing body, eligibility criteria, start/end dates, and tournament status. Distinct from season as tournaments have defined bracket structures and elimination logic.' .

ind:Bracket rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Bracket' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity capturing the bracket structure and real-time progression of a tournament — rounds, matchup slots, seeding positions, advancement rules, bye assignments, and results-driven slot filling. Tracks which fixture occupies each bracket slot, winner advancement logic, bracket reset rules for double-elimination formats, and conditional scheduling of future fixtures as results are confirmed. Enables real-time bracket visualization for broadcast overlays and fan engagement platforms.' .

ind:FixtureCalendar rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Fixture Calendar' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master scheduling entity representing the published fixture calendar for a season, league, or touring series. Captures calendar name, publication date, version number, scheduling authority, blackout dates, bye weeks, international window dates, and calendar status (draft, published, amended). Manages the official release of fixture schedules to downstream consumers including broadcast, ticketing, and venue operations. Distinct from individual fixture records — this is the calendar container.' .

ind:MatchResult rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Match Result' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity capturing the official outcome of a completed sports fixture — final scores, scorelines by period/quarter/half/set, overtime/shootout results, winning team/athlete, margin of victory, result status (official, under review, protested, forfeited), VAR/TMO intervention flag, and result confirmation timestamp. Serves as the SSOT for competitive outcomes used by league standings, broadcast highlights, and wagering integrations. Distinct from fixture (which is the scheduled event) — this is the recorded outcome.' .

ind:ScoringEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Scoring Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity capturing individual in-game scoring moments — goals, touchdowns, baskets, runs, points — with precise match clock time, period/quarter/half, athlete credited, assist attribution, scoring method (penalty, free kick, slam dunk, home run), VAR review flag, and score state after the event. Enables granular play-by-play data for broadcast overlays, content production, and fan engagement platforms. Feeds downstream content and broadcast domains.' .

ind:StatusHistory rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Status History' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Audit entity tracking every lifecycle state transition of a fixture — from announcement through completion or cancellation. Captures previous/new status, reason code (weather, force majeure, broadcast conflict, governing body directive), changed-by user, change timestamp, notification dispatch flag, proposed reschedule date(s), rescheduling workflow status, and financial impact flag for ticketing refund triggers. Serves as the complete postponement/rescheduling decision record and enables downstream systems to react to status changes in near-real-time.' .

ind:ProductionSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Production Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational entity managing the game-day/event-day production run-of-show for a fixture. Covers pre-event setup windows, doors-open coordination, pre-show entertainment, halftime/intermission programming (performer, duration, stage configuration, technical rider), post-event activities, and venue clearance timelines. Captures schedule version, production coordinator, broadcast go-live time, OB truck arrival, schedule lock timestamp, and sponsor activation windows. Serves as the execution plan distinct from fixture identity — owned by event production team.' .

ind:Participant rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Participant' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association entity linking athletes, teams, performers, or competing entities to a specific fixture. Captures participant role (home team, away team, headliner, support act, wildcard entry), seeding rank, participation status (confirmed, withdrawn, suspended, TBD), lineup submission timestamp, and captain/lead performer designation. Serves as the SSOT for who is participating in each event — consumed by broadcast, ticketing, content, and fan engagement domains.' .

ind:OfficiatingAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Officiating Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity managing the assignment of match officials — referees, linesmen, VAR operators, TMO (Television Match Official), judges, and scorers — to specific fixtures. Captures official role, assignment date, confirmation status, governing body certification level, conflict-of-interest flag, and post-match officiating report reference. Supports league governance, compliance with officiating standards (FIFA, NFL, NBA), and VAR/TMO review workflows.' .

ind:EventIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Event Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity recording significant in-event incidents requiring operational response — red cards, ejections, injuries requiring stoppage, crowd disturbances, equipment failures, weather delays (lightning, extreme heat), power outages, medical emergencies, and field/surface condition changes. Captures incident type, match clock time, severity level, response action taken, weather conditions at time of incident, regulatory reporting obligation flag (OSHA, governing body), resolution timestamp, and game-delay duration if applicable. Supports post-event reporting, safety compliance, and insurance documentation.' .

ind:VenueAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association entity linking a fixture to its assigned venue, capturing venue confirmation status, primary/alternate venue designation, venue configuration type (full capacity, reduced capacity, neutral site), ADA compliance confirmation, field/court/stage setup type, and assignment change history flag. Enables venue operations domain to prepare facility resources and ticketing domain to configure seating inventory for the specific event.' .

ind:CompetitionRound rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Competition Round' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference entity defining the rounds, stages, and phases within a season or tournament — Week 1, Matchday 3, Quarter-Final, Semi-Final, Wild Card Round, Conference Championship, Super Bowl, Group Stage, Knockout Round. Captures round name, round number, stage type, parent season or tournament reference, scheduled start/end dates, and number of fixtures in the round. Enables fixture scheduling, standings calculation, and bracket progression logic.' .

ind:PostEventReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Post Event Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional entity capturing the official post-event reconciliation record and formal closure document for each fixture. Includes final attendance figure, gross gate revenue, broadcast viewership estimate, incident summary count, officiating report reference, weather summary, production debrief notes, governing body submission status, report sign-off timestamp, and compliance checklist completion. Triggers downstream financial reconciliation, regulatory submissions (governing body match reports), content archival workflows, and sponsorship fulfillment confirmation.' .

ind:DigitalTouchpoint rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Digital Touchpoint' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master registry of all fan-facing digital channels operated by Sports Entertainment — mobile apps (iOS/Android), web portals, OTT streaming players, venue kiosk terminals, and IPTV endpoints. Each touchpoint has a unique identity, platform type, version lifecycle, supported capabilities (ticketing, merchandise, content, loyalty), SLA tier assignment, and operational status. SSOT for digital channel definitions referenced by all domains requiring channel-level attribution.' .

ind:FanAccount rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Platform-layer account representing a registered fan\'s digital identity on Sports Entertainment properties. Owns authentication credentials, account status (active/suspended/deactivated/merged), linked identity providers (SSO, social login, Apple/Google), account tier (free/premium/VIP), subscription flags, ARPU baseline, LTV score bucket, CAC attribution source, device limit policy, and omnichannel consent preference summary. Distinct from the fan domain\'s CRM profile — this entity owns the digital access layer, commercial relationship metrics, and platform-level account governance.' .

ind:AuthSession rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Auth Session' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each authenticated fan session across digital touchpoints. Captures session token, authentication method (password, SSO, biometric, social OAuth), device fingerprint, IP geolocation, session start/end timestamps, touchpoint channel, MFA status, session termination reason (logout, timeout, forced), and GDPR/CCPA consent version acknowledged at login. Supports SLA monitoring, fraud investigation, and GDPR right-to-erasure audit trails.' .

ind:FeatureEntitlement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Feature Entitlement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record defining which platform features, content assets, and capabilities a fan account is entitled to access — PPV streaming, premium content libraries, VIP lounge access, early ticket purchase windows, AR/VR experiences, and loyalty reward redemption. Captures entitlement source (subscription tier, PPV purchase, sponsor grant, loyalty milestone, promotional code), content/feature reference, effective dates, usage limits, geographic restrictions, DRM license type, concurrent access limits, and entitlement status. SSOT for all access control decisions across mobile, web, and OTT touchpoints.' .

ind:SlaPolicy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Sla Policy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference entity defining SLA commitments for each digital touchpoint and service tier — uptime targets (99.9% / 99.99%), response time thresholds, incident escalation windows, CDN failover SLAs, API availability commitments, and breach penalty definitions. Linked to touchpoint type, fan account tier, and partner API consumers. Supports SLA monitoring, breach alerting, and regulatory reporting for broadcast and OTT distribution agreements.' .

ind:SlaIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Sla Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each SLA breach or near-miss event across platform digital touchpoints. Captures incident type (downtime, latency breach, API timeout, CDN failure), affected touchpoint, impacted fan account count, breach duration, SLA policy violated, root cause classification, resolution timestamp, and post-incident review status. Feeds SLA compliance reporting and vendor penalty calculations for broadcast and OTT partners.' .

ind:ApiIntegration rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Api Integration' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master registry of all API integrations connecting the platform to internal systems and external partners — ticketing providers, CRM systems, commerce platforms, media asset management, and third-party data feeds. Captures integration name, protocol, authentication method, endpoint configuration, rate limits, data classification, SLA tier, health status, and owning team. SSOT for integration inventory supporting dependency mapping and incident triage.' .

ind:PersonalizationProfile rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Personalization Profile' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Platform-managed personalization record for each fan account, sourced from Adobe Experience Platform. Captures real-time segment memberships, preferred content genres (sport type, team affiliation, athlete follows), preferred touchpoint channel, notification preferences (push/email/SMS), language and locale, recommended content affinity scores, and last personalization engine sync timestamp. Distinct from the fan domain\'s CRM profile — this entity owns the digital behavioral personalization layer.' .

ind:FanSegment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Segment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference master of audience segments defined within the platform\'s personalization and CRM engines. Captures segment name, definition logic (behavioral, demographic, transactional), segment type (static/dynamic/AI-generated), owning business unit, activation channels, ARPU baseline, LTV tier, and GDPR processing basis. Includes segment membership records linking fan accounts to active segments with entry/exit tracking. Used for targeted engagement, sponsorship activation, and DTC campaign orchestration.' .

ind:DigitalSubscription rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Digital Subscription' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of a fan\'s active DTC digital subscription on Sports Entertainment platforms — OTT streaming passes, premium app tiers, PPV season packages, and bundled content+ticketing subscriptions. Captures subscription plan, billing cycle, start/renewal/expiry dates, auto-renew flag, payment method reference, ARPU contribution, promotional discount applied, cancellation reason, and churn risk tier. Sourced from Salesforce CRM subscription objects and Adobe Experience Platform entitlement data.' .

ind:FanInteraction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Interaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of meaningful fan actions across platform digital touchpoints — content plays, live stream joins, in-app purchases initiated, loyalty check-ins, poll/quiz participations, social shares, push notification engagements, and A/B test variant exposures. Captures interaction type, touchpoint channel, fan account reference, event/content reference, timestamp, session context, and outcome (completion, abandonment, conversion). Primary behavioral data feed for the personalization engine and engagement analytics. Scoped to platform-initiated interactions only; content consumption metrics owned by the content domain.' .

ind:NotificationCampaign rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Notification Campaign' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of platform-orchestrated omnichannel notification campaigns targeting fan segments — push notifications, in-app messages, SMS alerts, and email triggers for event reminders, ticket availability alerts, merchandise drops, loyalty milestones, and content recommendations. Captures campaign definition, target segment reference, channel mix, message templates, scheduling rules, personalization token mappings, A/B variant definitions, delivery metrics (sent/delivered/opened/clicked), and regulatory compliance status (CAN-SPAM, TCPA, ePrivacy). Distinct from sponsorship activation campaigns — this entity owns platform-to-fan direct communications only.' .

ind:DeviceRegistration rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Device Registration' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of fan-registered devices linked to a fan account for digital platform access — smartphones, tablets, smart TVs, gaming consoles, and connected wearables. Captures device type, OS platform and version, device fingerprint hash, push notification token, DRM device certificate, registration timestamp, last active timestamp, trusted device flag, and device limit enforcement status. Supports DRM concurrent stream enforcement, fraud detection, and personalized push notification delivery.' .

ind:AbTest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Ab Test' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of A/B and multivariate experiments running across platform digital touchpoints — UI/UX layout tests, personalization algorithm variants, pricing display experiments, notification copy tests, and feature rollout gates. Captures test hypothesis, target segment, variant definitions with traffic allocation percentages, success metrics and statistical significance thresholds, test lifecycle dates (draft/active/concluded/archived), and per-fan variant assignment records with exposure timestamps. Supports experiment governance, causal inference analysis, and GDPR Article 22 transparency for automated decision-making affecting fan experience.' .

ind:Roster rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Roster' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all athletes registered to a team or franchise within a league season. Tracks active, inactive, injured reserve (IR), practice squad, and waived status. Serves as the authoritative SSOT for athlete-team affiliation at any point in time, including jersey number, position designation, roster slot type, and activation dates. Critical for league operations, broadcast graphics, and ticketing systems.' .

ind:AthleteProfile rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Athlete Profile' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core master identity record for every athlete managed by Sports Entertainment. Stores biographical data (full legal name, preferred name, date of birth, nationality, country of origin), physical attributes (height, weight, dominant hand/foot), headshot image reference, social media handles, and career status (active, retired, suspended, deceased). This is the SSOT for athlete identity — all other athlete entities reference this record. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors talent module and league registration systems.' .

ind:AthleteContract rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Athlete Contract' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Athlete employment and service contracts governing the full lifecycle from initial signing through free agency. Tracks contract terms (compensation, duration, performance bonuses, trade clauses, option years, CBA-mandated terms), contract type (rookie, veteran, max, minimum, two-way), total value, guaranteed money, signing bonus, annual average value (AAV), and contract status (active, expired, voided, restructured). Includes free agency lifecycle: classification (UFA, RFA, ERFA, franchise tag, transition tag), qualifying offer amounts, tender amounts, right-of-first-refusal flags, free agency open date, signing deadline, and negotiation status. Integrates with SAP S/4HANA SD module for financial obligations and payroll processing via SAP SuccessFactors. Serves as the SSOT for an athlete\'s complete employment relationship from signing through free agency periods and re-signing.' .

ind:PerformanceStat rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Performance Stat' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Game-level and season-level performance statistics for athletes across all sports disciplines. Captures sport-specific metrics including WAR (Wins Above Replacement), ERA (Earned Run Average), QBR (Quarterback Rating), goals, assists, rebounds, tackles, saves, batting average, on-base percentage, and advanced analytics inputs. Sourced from SportsCode/Hudl performance analytics platform. Each record represents a statistical line for one athlete in one game or aggregated period, enabling broadcast overlays, fantasy sports feeds, and league standings calculations.' .

ind:InjuryRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Injury Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Clinical and operational record of athlete injuries, illnesses, and medical events throughout their career. Tracks injury type, body part affected, diagnosis code (ICD-10), injury date, expected return-to-play (RTP) date, actual RTP date, treatment protocol, treating physician, and impact on roster eligibility (IR designation, day-to-day, out). Supports OSHA compliance reporting, insurance claims, and broadcast injury updates. Managed in coordination with team medical staff systems.' .

ind:DraftSelection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Draft Selection' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of athlete selections made during league drafts (NFL Draft, NBA Draft, MLB Draft, MLS SuperDraft, etc.). Captures draft year, round number, overall pick number, selecting team, original team (if traded), draft class, pre-draft ranking, combine performance scores, and signing slot value per CBA. Tracks compensatory picks, traded picks, and conditional picks. Essential for league governance, salary cap management, and historical analytics.' .

ind:EligibilityStatus rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Eligibility Status' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Authoritative single source of truth for an athlete\'s current and historical eligibility to compete, encompassing all factors that grant or restrict participation rights. Covers: amateur/professional status, league registration, visa and work permit status, age eligibility, and all disciplinary actions including PED suspensions, conduct violations, game misconduct bans, and CBA disciplinary procedures. Tracks eligibility type, governing body (FIFA, NFL, NBA, WADA, CAS), effective/expiry dates, restriction details, suspension type and length (games, days, indefinite), financial penalties, issuing authority, reinstatement conditions, appeal status and outcomes, and chain of custody to originating doping test or incident. Critical for CBA compliance, international transfer regulations, WADA anti-doping enforcement, broadcast rights clearances, and real-time game-day eligibility verification. Replaces any separate suspension tracking — all disciplinary restrictions are eligibility events.' .

ind:NilAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Nil Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified commercial agreement record for all athlete brand partnerships, endorsements, and Name/Image/Likeness (NIL) deals. Covers both amateur/collegiate NIL agreements (subject to NCAA/conference NIL policies) and professional endorsement contracts (subject to CBA and league sponsor conflict rules). Tracks deal category (NIL-amateur, NIL-collegiate, professional endorsement, appearance, social media, licensing), brand partner, product category, deal value, contract duration, exclusivity scope, usage rights (broadcast, digital, social, in-venue), performance incentives, morality clause terms, disclosure status, and compliance with applicable regulations. Supports athlete commercial valuation, sponsorship conflict-of-interest checks, NIL compliance reporting, and broadcast rights clearances for athlete-branded content.' .

ind:AgentRelationship rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Agent Relationship' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association record linking athletes to their certified agents, agencies, and legal representatives. Tracks agent name, agency name, agent certification number (NFLPA, NBPA, MLBPA certified), representation scope (contract negotiation, endorsements, NIL, legal), relationship start date, termination date, commission rate, and power of attorney status. Supports contract negotiation workflows, communication routing, and compliance with league agent certification requirements.' .

ind:SuspensionRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Suspension Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Disciplinary suspension and ban records for athletes resulting from rule violations, anti-doping infractions, conduct violations, or CBA disciplinary procedures. Tracks suspension type (PED, conduct, game misconduct, league discipline), issuing authority, suspension length (games, days, indefinite), effective start and end dates, appeal status, reinstatement conditions, and financial penalties. Distinct from injury-related roster designations — suspensions are disciplinary actions with legal and compliance implications.' .

ind:CombineResult rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Combine Result' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Pre-draft combine and scouting evaluation results for prospective athletes. Captures combine event (NFL Scouting Combine, NBA Draft Combine, MLB Draft), measurement date, physical measurements (height, weight, wingspan, hand size), athletic test results (40-yard dash, vertical jump, bench press reps, shuttle drill, 3-cone drill, 60-yard dash, lane agility), position-specific drills, and composite score. Sourced from SportsCode/Hudl evaluation platform. Feeds draft selection decisions and contract slot value calculations.' .

ind:ScoutingReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Scouting Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Comprehensive pre-draft evaluation record combining quantitative combine measurables and qualitative scout assessments for prospective athletes. Captures combine event participation (NFL Scouting Combine, NBA Draft Combine, MLB Draft, pro days), physical measurements (height, weight, wingspan, hand size), athletic test results (40-yard dash, vertical jump, bench press reps, shuttle drill, 3-cone drill, 60-yard dash, lane agility), position-specific drill scores, composite scores, and overall grade (OVR). Includes scout narrative evaluations (strengths, weaknesses, projection tier, comparable player), evaluation type (combine measurables, scout assessment, video analysis, pro day), evaluator identity, and draft recommendation. Sourced from SportsCode/Hudl evaluation platform. Feeds draft boards, free agency targeting, trade evaluation, and contract slot value calculations.' .

ind:AwardHonor rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Award Honor' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified record of all athlete achievements, awards, honors, career milestones, and recognitions across their professional lifecycle. Covers: league awards (MVP, Cy Young, Ballon d\'Or, All-Star, All-Pro, Rookie of the Year), career records (all-time scoring leader, consecutive games streak), career lifecycle events (debut, first goal/touchdown/hit, 100th cap, retirement, Hall of Fame induction, contract extension, trade milestone), and fan/media recognitions. Tracks achievement type (award, milestone, record, induction, career_event), awarding/certifying body, date, sport, league, team at time of achievement, statistical context, voting details where applicable, and broadcast highlight reference. Supports content production, broadcast storytelling, merchandise licensing, athlete commercial valuation, fan engagement platforms, and historical archives.' .

ind:SalaryCapEntry rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Salary Cap Entry' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Athlete-level salary cap accounting records tracking how each contract contributes to a team\'s league-mandated salary cap. Captures cap year, base salary cap hit, signing bonus proration, dead cap value, incentive escalators (likely/unlikely per CBA), cap relief from restructures, and cap hold for restricted free agents. Integrates with SAP S/4HANA FI/CO for financial reporting and Workday Adaptive Planning for cap forecasting. Distinct from the contract master — this is the annual cap accounting view.' .

ind:FreeAgencyStatus rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'Free Agency Status' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Tracks an athlete\'s free agency eligibility, classification, and market activity during free agency periods. Captures free agency type (unrestricted/UFA, restricted/RFA, exclusive rights/ERFA, franchise tag, transition tag), qualifying offer amount, tender amount, original team right of first refusal flag, free agency open date, signing deadline, and current negotiation status. Supports roster planning, salary cap management, and broadcast transaction reporting.' .

ind:InternationalCap rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Athlete ;
    rdfs:label 'International Cap' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of an athlete\'s appearances representing a national team or international governing body in sanctioned international competitions (FIFA World Cup qualifiers, Olympic Games, international friendlies, Six Nations, etc.). Captures cap number, competition name, opponent, match date, result, goals/points scored, minutes played, captain flag, and governing body (FIFA, World Rugby, FIBA, IOC). Distinct from club/franchise performance_stat — international caps have separate eligibility and nationality rules.' .

ind:GlAccount rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Gl Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'General ledger account master record defining a specific financial classification node within the enterprise chart of accounts. Each GL account represents a unique posting target (e.g., ticket revenue, broadcast rights income, venue operating expense, player salary, naming rights deferred revenue). Stores account number, description, account type (P&L vs balance sheet), currency, tax category, reconciliation account flag, cost element category, account group, and posting block status. SSOT for all account classification, financial statement line mapping, and cost element definitions across all Sports Entertainment legal entities in SAP S/4HANA FI.' .

ind:CostCenter rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Cost Center' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SAP CO cost center master representing an organizational unit responsible for incurring costs — e.g., venue operations, broadcast production, athlete performance, league administration, merchandise fulfillment. Tracks cost center hierarchy, responsible manager, controlling area, validity period, and budget allocation. SSOT for cost accountability across all Sports Entertainment business units.' .

ind:ProfitCenter rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Profit Center' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SAP CO profit center master representing a revenue-generating business unit — e.g., a specific league franchise, venue, OTT streaming platform, or merchandise line. Enables EBITDA reporting and profitability analysis at the business segment level. Stores profit center hierarchy, controlling area, company code assignment, and segment classification.' .

ind:CompanyCode rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Company Code' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Legal entity master record within the SAP S/4HANA organizational structure. Represents each incorporated Sports Entertainment subsidiary or operating company (e.g., league operating company, broadcast network entity, venue management LLC). Stores company code, legal name, country, currency, fiscal year variant, and chart of accounts assignment. Required for SOX-compliant intercompany and SEC reporting.' .

ind:JournalEntry rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Journal Entry' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core financial posting document in SAP FI representing a balanced double-entry accounting transaction with embedded line items (posting rows). Each journal entry contains one or more line items specifying GL account, amount, debit/credit indicator, cost center, profit center, and tax code. Captures document type (invoice, payment, accrual, intercompany, allocation), posting date, fiscal period, company code, reference document, posting user, reversal indicator, and SOX approval workflow status. SSOT for all financial movements across the general ledger including revenue recognition postings for ticket sales, broadcast rights, sponsorship, merchandise, and cost allocation postings. Line-item granularity is embedded within this product — no separate line product exists.' .

ind:Budget rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Budget' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Financial planning record encompassing annual budgets, multi-year plans, and rolling forecasts per cost center, profit center, or WBS element. Managed in Workday Adaptive Planning and loaded into SAP CO. Captures budget/forecast version (original, revised, Q1-Q4 reforecast), scenario type (base, upside, downside), budget type (OPEX, CAPEX), fiscal year/period, planned amounts by GL account and cost element at monthly/quarterly granularity, committed amounts, actuals-to-date, and approval workflow status. Supports FP&A variance analysis, rolling forecast cycles, EBITDA projections, and investor relations guidance for Sports Entertainment.' .

ind:WbsElement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Wbs Element' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Project and activity cost collection object in SAP CO representing hierarchical project nodes (WBS elements) and simple cost collectors (internal orders). Covers capital projects (venue construction, broadcast infrastructure upgrades, digital platform builds) and short-term operational activities (event productions, marketing campaigns, athlete signing bonuses). Stores WBS/order code, project definition, order type, responsible cost center, planned/actual costs, settlement rule, billing element flag, budget, and status (created, released, technically complete, closed). Supports CAPEX tracking, asset-under-construction accounting, and activity-level P&L analysis.' .

ind:ArInvoice rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Ar Invoice' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Accounts receivable invoice issued to external customers — sponsors, broadcast rights licensees, merchandise wholesale buyers, and premium suite holders. Stores invoice number, billing date, due date, customer account, payment terms, gross amount, tax amount, net amount, currency, payment status, and dunning level. Managed in SAP FI-AR. SSOT for revenue billing documents.' .

ind:ApInvoice rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Ap Invoice' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Accounts payable invoice received from vendors and suppliers — venue service contractors, broadcast equipment providers, athlete agents, merchandise manufacturers. Stores vendor invoice number, receipt date, posting date, vendor account, payment terms, gross amount, tax amount, net amount, currency, three-way match status (PO/GR/IR), and payment block reason. Managed in SAP FI-AP.' .

ind:Payment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Payment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Financial payment transaction recording the settlement of accounts receivable and accounts payable obligations. Captures payment document number, payment date, payment method (ACH, wire, check, card, digital wallet), bank account, cleared invoice references, payment amount, currency, exchange rate, clearing document number, and payment run ID. Covers outbound vendor disbursements, inbound customer receipts, and automated payment program runs in SAP FI. Links to AR invoices (customer receipts) and AP invoices (vendor payments) for complete cash application and reconciliation.' .

ind:FixedAsset rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Fixed Asset' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Fixed asset master record in SAP FI-AA representing capitalized physical and intangible assets — stadium structures, broadcast towers, OB trucks, scoreboards, digital platform infrastructure, and acquired broadcast rights. Stores asset class, acquisition date, acquisition cost, useful life, depreciation method, accumulated depreciation, net book value, and disposal status. SSOT for CAPEX and depreciation accounting.' .

ind:IntercompanySettlement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Intercompany Settlement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Intercompany financial transaction capturing settlements between Sports Entertainment legal entities for transfer pricing, shared services, and rights licensing. Examples: broadcast rights fees from network entity to league entity, shared services charges from corporate to venue subsidiaries, NIL licensing fees between athlete management and franchise entities, and content licensing between streaming platform and production entities. Stores sending company code, receiving company code, transaction type, settlement amount, currency, netting agreement reference, netting status, elimination flag for consolidated reporting, and posting period. Required for SEC consolidated financial statement eliminations and transfer pricing documentation.' .

ind:RevenueRecognitionSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Revenue Recognition Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Revenue recognition schedule governing when and how deferred revenue is recognized into earned revenue per ASC 606 / IFRS 15 standards. Applies to multi-year broadcast rights contracts, season ticket packages, multi-event sponsorship deals, and long-term naming rights agreements. Stores contract reference, performance obligation description, total contract value, deferred balance, recognition method (straight-line, milestone, usage-based), recognition start/end dates, period recognition amounts, and cumulative recognized amount. SSOT for ASC 606 compliance, deferred revenue waterfall reporting, and period-end revenue recognition journal entry generation. Distinct from recurring_revenue which tracks commercial ARR/churn metrics — this product owns the accounting treatment and timing of revenue recognition.' .

ind:SoxControl rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Sox Control' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SOX internal control and period-end governance record documenting financial controls required under Sarbanes-Oxley Section 302/404 for publicly traded Sports Entertainment entities. Encompasses standing controls (segregation of duties, approval thresholds, system access reviews) and period-end close activities (accrual postings, depreciation runs, intercompany eliminations, financial statement preparation, flux analysis). Stores control ID, control objective, control type (preventive/detective/corrective), frequency (continuous/daily/monthly/quarterly/annual), responsible owner, due date, completion date, testing method, last test date, test result, deficiency classification (significant deficiency/material weakness), remediation status, and sign-off approver. SSOT for external auditor evidence packages, management representation letters, and SOX-compliant close governance aligned to SEC 10-Q/10-K reporting deadlines.' .

ind:RecurringRevenue rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Recurring Revenue' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR) tracking record for subscription-based and recurring revenue streams — OTT streaming subscriptions, season ticket memberships, multi-year sponsorship contracts, and broadcast rights agreements. Stores ARR component type, contract reference, subscriber/partner count, MRR, ARR, churn amount, expansion amount, net ARR movement, and reporting period. SSOT for DTC and investor ARR/ARPU/churn metrics and disclosures. Distinct from revenue_recognition_schedule which governs ASC 606 accounting treatment — this product owns the commercial ARR metrics used in investor relations, board reporting, and subscription business KPIs.' .

ind:Facility rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Facility' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for every physical venue asset — stadiums, arenas, amphitheaters, and concert halls — owned or operated by Sports Entertainment. Captures venue name, full address, geo-coordinates, venue type (stadium/arena/amphitheater/ballpark), playing surface type, roof type (open/retractable/enclosed), year built, year last renovated, total gross square footage, ownership structure (owned/leased/managed), primary sport or entertainment category, home team or resident tenant, ADA compliance certification status, OSHA safety rating, ISO 20121 sustainability certification, seating bowl configuration code, naming rights holder, time zone, and operational status (active/mothballed/under-renovation/decommissioned). Serves as the SSOT for all venue identity and physical characteristics consumed by event scheduling, ticketing inventory, and broadcast production planning.' .

ind:SeatingSection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Seating Section' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines every named seating section within a facility — bowl sections, club levels, suites, GA standing areas, SRO zones, press boxes, and accessible seating blocks. Attributes include section code, section name, level (lower/club/upper/field), section type (reserved/GA/SRO/suite/accessible), row count, seat count per row, total capacity, ADA-accessible seat count, sightline rating, price zone code, and whether the section is covered. Sourced from Archtics Venue Seating and Inventory Management.' .

ind:Seat rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Seat' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Atomic seat-level inventory record for every individual seat within a seating section. Captures seat number, row identifier, seat type (standard/accessible/companion/premium/stool), physical coordinates (row-seat position), ADA designation flag, obstructed-view flag, aisle seat flag, kill-seat flag (structurally unavailable), current operational status (active/inactive/hold/kill), and last inspection date. Serves as the SSOT for seat-level inventory consumed by the ticketing domain.' .

ind:CapacityConfig rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Capacity Config' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Event-specific or configuration-specific capacity setup for a facility, capturing how total capacity is allocated across seating modes for a given event type or configuration profile. Attributes include configuration name, event type applicability (concert/sports/mixed), total configured capacity, GA capacity, reserved capacity, suite capacity, accessible capacity, press/media capacity, field/floor capacity, kill-seat count, and configuration effective date range. Enables dynamic capacity management across different event formats (e.g., end-stage concert vs. full-bowl sports).' .

ind:ParkingLot rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Parking Lot' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all parking facilities associated with a venue — surface lots, structured garages, VIP lots, accessible parking areas, and remote shuttle lots. Captures lot name, lot code, lot type (surface/garage/remote/VIP/accessible), total spaces, accessible spaces, EV charging spaces, distance from main entrance (meters), managed-by party reference, pricing tier, and operational status. Supports event-day parking logistics, revenue management, and ADA compliance reporting.' .

ind:BmsSystem rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Bms System' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for Building Management System (BMS) subsystems installed within a facility — HVAC units, electrical distribution panels, fire suppression systems, lighting control systems, plumbing networks, and security/access control systems. Attributes include system name, system type (HVAC/electrical/fire/lighting/plumbing/security), manufacturer, model number, installation date, last certification date, next scheduled maintenance date, operational status, and responsible maintenance team. Serves as the SSOT for facility infrastructure assets tracked against OSHA and local building code compliance.' .

ind:MaintenanceWorkOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Maintenance Work Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record capturing every planned or reactive maintenance activity performed on facility infrastructure, BMS systems, seating, concourse equipment, or structural elements. Attributes include work order number, work order type (preventive/corrective/emergency/inspection), priority level, asset or system reference, description of work, requested date, scheduled start/end date, actual start/end date, technician assignment, labor hours, parts used, estimated cost, actual cost, completion status, and sign-off by facility manager. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA Plant Maintenance (PM) module.' .

ind:SafetyInspection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Safety Inspection' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Records all formal safety and compliance inspections conducted at a facility, including OSHA walkthroughs, fire marshal inspections, ADA accessibility audits, structural engineering assessments, and ISO 20121 sustainability audits. Attributes include inspection type, inspection date, inspector name and credentials, regulatory body (OSHA/ADA/fire marshal/local authority), areas inspected, findings count, critical findings count, corrective actions required, corrective action due date, pass/fail outcome, and certificate issued flag. Supports regulatory reporting and compliance tracking.' .

ind:SafetyIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Safety Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Captures every safety or security incident occurring at a venue — fan injuries, worker accidents, medical emergencies, structural failures, fire alarms, crowd disturbances, and security breaches. Attributes include incident date/time, incident type, location within venue (section/zone/lot), severity level (minor/moderate/serious/critical), number of persons affected, emergency services called flag, OSHA recordable flag, incident description, immediate response actions taken, root cause, corrective action plan, and incident closure date. Mandatory for OSHA 300 log compliance and insurance reporting.' .

ind:EventDayOps rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Event Day Ops' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational readiness, execution, and closeout record for each event held at a venue, capturing the full event-day lifecycle from pre-event certification through post-event reconciliation. Pre-event readiness attributes include checklist completion status, checklist version, HVAC/fire/emergency system verification, security sweep completion, ADA access confirmation, medical station readiness, critical-item failure count, overall readiness status (approved/conditional/rejected), and facility manager approval with timestamp. Execution attributes include gates-open/close times, load-in/load-out windows, actual attendance, peak concourse occupancy, active concession stand count, active parking lot count, security and medical staffing counts, weather conditions, and incident count. Post-event attributes include operational status (pre-event/in-progress/post-event/closed), damage assessment flag, and facility manager sign-off. Distinct from the event domain\'s event record — this is the venue\'s operational execution layer owning the single source of truth for event-day readiness certification and operational performance.' .

ind:ConcessionStand rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Concession Stand' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record and POS-level transactional detail for individual concession stand units within a facility — food and beverage outlets, portable carts, premium club kitchens, and bar stations. Master attributes include stand name, stand code, stand type (permanent/portable/premium/bar/specialty), concourse location, cuisine/product category (hot food/cold beverage/alcohol/snack/merchandise), operator name (in-house/third-party concessionaire), POS terminal count, seating capacity (if applicable), ADA-accessible service counter flag, health inspection status, and operational status. Transaction-level attributes include transaction date/time, event reference, POS terminal ID, item SKU, item description, quantity sold, unit price, discount applied, gross amount, tax amount, net amount, payment method (cash/card/mobile), and void flag. Supports per-event concession revenue reporting, per-capita spend analysis, top-selling item tracking, and health/safety compliance. Sourced from POS systems integrated with SAP S/4HANA SD.' .

ind:ConcessionTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Concession Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'POS-level transactional record for every food, beverage, and non-merchandise sale made at a concession stand or portable cart during an event. Attributes include transaction date/time, stand reference, event reference, POS terminal ID, item SKU, item description, quantity sold, unit price, discount applied, gross amount, tax amount, net amount, payment method (cash/card/mobile), and void flag. Sourced from POS systems integrated with SAP S/4HANA SD. Enables per-event concession revenue reporting and per-capita spend analysis.' .

ind:Suite rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Suite' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for premium hospitality suites and club boxes within a facility, encompassing physical configuration, amenities, and the full commercial license/lease lifecycle. Physical attributes include suite name, suite number, suite type (private suite/club box/loge box/party suite/press box), level, total capacity, seat count, standing positions, square footage, amenity list (private bar/catering kitchen/AV system/private restroom), and ADA-accessible flag. Commercial license attributes include license number, licensee name, licensee type (corporate/individual), license start/end dates, term (annual/multi-year/per-event), total license fee, payment schedule, included event types and count, catering credit amount, parking passes included, renewal option flag, contract status (active/expired/terminated/pending), and lease pipeline stage. Supports suite revenue management, premium hospitality operations, lease renewal pipeline tracking, and per-suite P&L analysis. Distinct from sponsorship domain partnership contracts — this is a venue-specific hospitality revenue instrument.' .

ind:SuiteLicense rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Suite License' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Commercial agreement record for the licensing or leasing of a premium suite or club box to a corporate or individual client. Attributes include license number, suite reference, licensee name, licensee type (corporate/individual), license start date, license end date, term (annual/multi-year/per-event), total license fee, payment schedule, included event types, included event count, catering credit amount, parking passes included, renewal option flag, and contract status (active/expired/terminated/pending). Distinct from the sponsorship domain\'s partnership contracts — this is a venue-specific hospitality revenue instrument.' .

ind:AccessibilityFeature rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Accessibility Feature' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Catalog of ADA and accessibility features installed or available at a facility — wheelchair ramps, elevator banks, accessible restrooms, hearing loop systems, braille signage, accessible parking spaces, companion seating areas, and sensory rooms. Attributes include feature name, feature type, location description, quantity/count, installation date, last inspection date, compliance standard (ADA/local code), compliance status (compliant/non-compliant/remediation-in-progress), and responsible maintenance team. Supports ADA compliance reporting and fan accessibility experience management.' .

ind:Rental rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Rental' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record for third-party venue rental agreements — non-resident events such as concerts, corporate events, graduations, and private functions booked at a Sports Entertainment facility. Attributes include rental agreement number, renter name, renter type (promoter/corporate/private/government), event name, event type, rental start date/time, rental end date/time, spaces rented (full venue/partial/specific zones), base rental fee, ancillary service fees (AV/catering/security/cleaning), total contract value, deposit amount, deposit received date, payment status, and rental status (inquiry/confirmed/in-progress/completed/cancelled).' .

ind:OperationalReadiness rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Operational Readiness' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Pre-event checklist and readiness certification record confirming that a facility has met all operational, safety, and compliance requirements before gates open for an event. Attributes include readiness assessment date/time, event reference, facility reference, checklist version, number of checklist items, items passed, items failed, items waived, critical items failed count, HVAC system status, fire suppression system status, emergency lighting status, medical station readiness status, security sweep completion flag, ADA access verification flag, overall readiness status (approved/conditional/rejected), and approving facility manager.' .

ind:League rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'League' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for each professional sports league or governing body (NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS, FIFA, IOC, etc.). Captures league identity, founding year, sport type, governing body affiliation, headquarters, official name, acronym, active status, and league-level configuration such as number of teams, playoff format, and championship structure. This is the SSOT for league identity across the enterprise.' .

ind:Conference rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Conference' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Organizational subdivision of a league representing a conference or association grouping (e.g., AFC/NFC in NFL, Eastern/Western Conference in NBA, American/National League in MLB). Tracks conference name, abbreviation, parent league, geographic alignment, number of divisions, and active season range. Supports standings aggregation and playoff seeding logic.' .

ind:Division rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Division' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Sub-grouping within a conference representing a competitive division (e.g., NFC East, AL Central, Atlantic Division). Stores division name, abbreviation, parent conference, parent league, geographic region, number of member teams, and active status. Drives divisional standings, scheduling rules, and playoff qualification criteria.' .

ind:Franchise rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Franchise' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for each team franchise holding a league membership license, including the governing franchise agreement terms. Captures franchise legal name, market city/metro area, team nickname, abbreviation, founding year, ownership entity reference, home venue reference, current league and division membership, historical relocation records, expansion/original franchise flag, franchise valuation estimate, active/suspended/defunct status, and CBA participation flag. Also stores franchise agreement terms: territorial rights, revenue sharing obligations, relocation restrictions, expansion fees, ownership transfer rules, agreement version, execution date, governing CBA reference, and amendment history. Tracks official roster filing snapshots (active roster count, IR, practice squad, compliance status) at points in time. SSOT for franchise identity, membership governance, and roster compliance.' .

ind:Season rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Season' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines a competitive season calendar and postseason structure for a league. Captures season year, season type (regular, preseason, postseason), official start and end dates, number of scheduled games per team, salary cap year flag, CBA governing version, and season status (upcoming, active, completed). Includes playoff/postseason bracket definition: bracket format (single elimination, best-of-series), number of rounds, seeding methodology, bye rules, home-court/field advantage rules, bracket position assignments per franchise, advancement status, and series results through each round to championship. Anchors all scheduling, standings, draft, and compliance calculations.' .

ind:LeagueSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'League Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Official league-published game schedule record linking two franchises to a specific date, time, venue, and season week/round/matchday. Includes home/away designation, broadcast window assignment, game type (regular season, playoff, neutral site, exhibition), scheduling status (confirmed, postponed, cancelled, rescheduled), original vs. revised date tracking, and transaction window compliance flag. Serves as the planning backbone for event operations, broadcast scheduling, and standings calculations.' .

ind:Standing rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Standing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic snapshot of competitive standings for a franchise within a division, conference, and league for a given season. Tracks wins, losses, ties/draws, overtime losses, points (hockey/soccer), winning percentage, games behind leader, home/away/divisional/conference records, goal/run/point differential, current streak, last-10 record, strength of schedule, clinch/elimination status, and standings rank. Updated after each official game result. Drives playoff qualification logic and tiebreaker resolution.' .

ind:PlayoffBracket rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Playoff Bracket' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines the postseason bracket structure for a league season, including bracket format (single elimination, best-of-series), number of rounds, seeding methodology, bye rules, home-court/field advantage rules, and bracket position assignments per franchise. Tracks advancement status and series results through each round to championship.' .

ind:GameResult rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Game Result' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Official final result record for a completed scheduled game. Captures final score by team, overtime periods played, winning/losing franchise, result type (regulation, OT, SO, forfeit), official attendance, weather conditions (outdoor venues), VAR/TMO intervention flag, protest flag, and result certification status. SSOT for official game outcomes used in standings calculations.' .

ind:OfficiatingCrew rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Officiating Crew' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for game officials and their crew assignments. At the individual level, captures official name, badge number, officiating body, certification tier, sport specialization, years of experience, geographic assignment region, contract type, and active status. At the crew assignment level, tracks crew composition (crew chief, referee, umpires, linesmen, VAR operator, TMO), game reference, assignment date, and post-game performance evaluation status. Supports officiating quality management, conflict-of-interest screening, and CBA compliance for officials\' unions.' .

ind:Official rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Official' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for an individual game official (referee, umpire, linesman, VAR operator, TMO, line judge). Captures official name, badge number, officiating body, certification tier, sport specialization, active status, years of experience, geographic assignment region, and contract type. Distinct from athlete and workforce domains — officials are governed by league officiating bureaus.' .

ind:DisciplinaryAction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Disciplinary Action' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of a formal disciplinary action issued by the league against a player, coach, franchise, or official. Includes infraction type (suspension, fine, ejection, probation, loss of draft pick), subject entity type and reference, incident date, game reference, ruling date, penalty amount, suspension length in games, appeal eligibility, appeal status, and final ruling. Supports competitive integrity and CBA compliance tracking.' .

ind:CbaAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Cba Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for a Collective Bargaining Agreement between a league and its players association or officials union. Tracks CBA name, effective date range, signatory parties, salary cap floor/ceiling by year, minimum salary schedule, revenue sharing formula, free agency eligibility rules, arbitration provisions, grievance procedures, drug testing protocols, player safety provisions, retirement/pension terms, and ratification status. SSOT for labor relations governance — referenced by salary_cap, franchise_agreement, and disciplinary_action for rule authority.' .

ind:SalaryCap rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Salary Cap' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Annual salary cap definition and franchise compliance tracking per league and season. Defines hard cap, soft cap, luxury tax threshold, cap floor, and applicable exceptions (mid-level, bi-annual, franchise tag). Tracks cap year, total league revenue basis, escrow percentage, cap calculation methodology, and official announcement date. Also captures per-franchise compliance snapshots: total active payroll, cap space remaining, dead cap, injured reserve credits, practice squad charges, cap holds, luxury tax liability, and compliance status (compliant, warning, violation). Updated on roster transactions and contract signings. SSOT for salary cap rules AND franchise-level cap compliance.' .

ind:CapCompliance rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Cap Compliance' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record tracking a franchise\'s salary cap compliance position at a point in time within a season. Captures total active payroll, cap space remaining, dead cap amount, injured reserve credits, practice squad charges, cap holds, luxury tax liability, and compliance status (compliant, warning, violation). Updated on roster transactions and contract signings.' .

ind:Draft rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Draft' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for a league player draft event and all individual pick selections. At the event level: draft year, sport, number of rounds, total picks, draft format (live, virtual, hybrid), draft date and location, eligibility class (college, international, supplemental), draft order determination method (lottery, inverse standings, coin flip), and draft status. At the pick level: round number, overall pick number, current owning franchise, original owning franchise (if traded), full trade history chain, compensatory/conditional pick flags, pick protection level (top-N protected), pick status (available, traded, exercised, forfeited, voided), and selected athlete reference upon exercise. Supports draft asset management, trade analysis, and future pick valuation models.' .

ind:DraftPick rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Draft Pick' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual draft pick record within a draft event, tracking round number, overall pick number, current owning franchise, original owning franchise (if traded), full trade history chain, compensatory pick flag, conditional pick flag with conditions description, pick protection level (top-N protected), pick status (available, traded, exercised, forfeited, voided), and selected athlete reference upon exercise. Supports draft asset management, trade analysis, and future pick valuation models.' .

ind:FranchiseAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Franchise Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Legal franchise membership agreement between the league and a franchise owner, defining territorial rights, revenue sharing obligations, relocation restrictions, expansion fees, ownership transfer rules, compliance obligations, and term dates. Tracks agreement version, execution date, governing CBA reference, and amendment history. Distinct from athlete contracts — this governs franchise-level league membership.' .

ind:TradeTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Trade Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of inter-franchise player and asset movement including trades, waiver claims, and waiver wire transactions. Captures transaction date, involved franchises, assets exchanged (player references, draft pick references, cash considerations), transaction type (trade, waiver claim, waiver placement, DFA assignment), league approval status, approval date, voiding conditions, transaction window compliance flag, waiver priority order, salary obligation transfer details, and clearing dates. SSOT for all inter-franchise roster movement requiring league approval.' .

ind:WaiverClaim rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Waiver Claim' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of a franchise placing a player on waivers or claiming a player off waivers. Tracks player reference, placing franchise, claiming franchise, waiver type (unconditional, conditional, DFA), waiver wire order priority, claim date, claim status (unclaimed, claimed, revoked), salary obligation transfer, and clearing date. Supports roster management and cap compliance workflows.' .

ind:RosterFiling rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Roster Filing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Official league-certified roster snapshot for a franchise at a specific point in time within a season. Captures roster date, franchise reference, season reference, active roster count, injured reserve count, practice squad count, 40-man roster count (MLB), two-way contract count, roster compliance status, and submission timestamp. Distinct from athlete master — this is the official league-filed roster document.' .

ind:Vendor rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all external vendors, suppliers, and third-party contractors engaged by Sports Entertainment. SSOT for vendor identity including legal entity name, tax ID (EIN/VAT), business classification (broadcast partner, venue service provider, merchandise supplier, technology vendor, contractor), registration status, diversity certifications (MBE/WBE/DBE), preferred vendor tier (strategic/preferred/approved/probation), category classification with hierarchical taxonomy (Broadcast Technology, Venue Facilities, Merchandise Manufacturing, IT Infrastructure, Catering, Security, Transportation, Medical), primary contact details, banking information for payment disbursement, onboarding date, and risk tier. SSOT for vendor categorization — no separate category reference table. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA MM vendor master.' .

ind:VendorContact rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Contact' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual contact persons associated with a vendor organization serving Sports Entertainment — account managers, technical leads for broadcast integration, legal representatives for contract negotiations, on-site supervisors for venue services, and escalation contacts for SLA breaches. Tracks name, title, role type (commercial, technical, legal, operational), phone, email, preferred communication channel, timezone, language preference, and active status. Supports relationship management, SLA escalation routing, and event-day coordination workflows.' .

ind:VendorContract rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Contract' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational supply-side commercial agreements between Sports Entertainment and its vendors, including full lifecycle management. Captures contract number, type (MSA, SOW, NDA, framework agreement), effective/expiration dates, auto-renewal terms, total contract value (TCV), currency, payment terms, governing law jurisdiction, termination notice period, and status. Owns complete amendment history (amendment number, type, scope changes, price adjustments, term extensions, financial impact delta, approval authority, SOX audit trail) and renewal lifecycle (renewal trigger dates, renewal type — auto-renewal/renegotiated/terminated, revised terms, new TCV, approval status). SSOT for all contract modifications and renewals. Distinct from sponsorship agreements (revenue-generating) — covers cost-side vendor obligations. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA SD/MM contract management.' .

ind:SlaDefinition rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Sla Definition' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Service Level Agreement definitions governing vendor performance obligations. Captures SLA code, service category, metric type (uptime %, response time, delivery lead time, resolution time), target threshold, critical threshold, measurement frequency, penalty structure for breach, and applicable contract reference. Used for broadcast uptime SLAs, venue HVAC maintenance SLAs, IT infrastructure SLAs, and catering delivery SLAs.' .

ind:SlaMeasurement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Sla Measurement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic SLA performance measurement records capturing actual vendor performance against agreed thresholds for Sports Entertainment operations. Records measurement period (daily/weekly/monthly/per-event), actual metric value, target value, variance percentage, breach flag, breach severity (minor/major/critical), consecutive breach count, measurement source system (network monitoring, IoT sensors, manual inspection), and auto-generated penalty trigger. Covers broadcast uptime measurements during live events, venue HVAC response times, catering delivery punctuality, and security deployment readiness. Feeds vendor performance scorecards and automated penalty calculation workflows.' .

ind:PurchaseOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Purchase Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Formal procurement purchase orders issued to vendors for goods and services including line-item detail (material/service, quantity, unit price, delivery schedule, goods receipt quantity, invoice verification status). Captures PO number, PO type (standard, blanket, emergency), order date, requested delivery date, delivery address (venue or facility), total order value, currency, payment terms, approval status, and goods receipt status. Supports three-way matching (PO/goods receipt/invoice) for accounts payable processing. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA MM purchasing module (EKKO/EKPO). Covers procurement for venue operations, broadcast equipment, merchandise inventory, and event services.' .

ind:PartnerGoodsReceipt rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Partner Goods Receipt' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Records of physical or digital goods and services received from vendors against purchase orders at Sports Entertainment facilities. Captures receipt date, receiving location (stadium, arena, concert venue, warehouse, broadcast facility), received quantity, accepted quantity, rejected quantity, rejection reason code, quality inspection result (pass/conditional/fail), inspector name, and SAP posting status. Covers merchandise inventory receipts, broadcast equipment deliveries, venue maintenance supplies, event production materials, and catering provisions. Enables three-way matching (PO/GR/Invoice) and triggers accounts payable invoice verification.' .

ind:VendorInvoice rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Invoice' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Vendor-submitted invoices for goods and services delivered to Sports Entertainment. Captures invoice number, invoice date, billing period, gross amount, tax amount, net amount, currency, payment due date, early payment discount terms, three-way match status (PO/GR/Invoice), approval status, and payment block reason. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA FI Accounts Payable (RBKP/RSEG). Distinct from fan-facing or sponsor invoices owned by other domains.' .

ind:VendorPayment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Payment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Payment transactions disbursed to vendors against approved invoices. Captures payment date, payment method (ACH, wire, check, virtual card), payment amount, currency, bank account reference, payment run ID, clearing document number, and payment status. Sourced from SAP S/4HANA FI payment run (F110). Supports cash flow management, EBITDA reporting, and vendor relationship management.' .

ind:Rfp rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Rfp' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Request for Proposal records issued to prospective vendors during competitive procurement processes. Captures RFP number, title, procurement category, issuing department, issue date, submission deadline, evaluation criteria, estimated contract value, number of vendors invited, and RFP status (draft, issued, evaluation, awarded, cancelled). Supports strategic sourcing for broadcast technology, venue services, merchandise manufacturing, and IT platform procurement.' .

ind:RfpResponse rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Rfp Response' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Vendor bid submissions in response to issued RFPs. Captures responding vendor, submission date, proposed price, proposed delivery timeline, technical compliance score, commercial compliance score, evaluator notes, shortlist flag, and award recommendation. Enables competitive bid evaluation and vendor selection documentation for procurement governance and audit trails.' .

ind:VendorScorecard rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Scorecard' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic vendor performance evaluation records assessing quality, delivery, responsiveness, SLA compliance, and commercial value. Captures evaluation period, overall score, sub-scores by dimension (quality, delivery, service, innovation, compliance), evaluator, evaluation method (automated/manual), performance tier (preferred/approved/probation/disqualified), and recommended action. Drives vendor tiering decisions and contract renewal negotiations.' .

ind:ServiceOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Service Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Work orders issued to vendors for delivery of specific services at Sports Entertainment venues and events — broadcast setup/teardown, LED scoreboard maintenance, HVAC and plumbing maintenance, security deployment and crowd management, catering and hospitality, ground transportation and logistics, stage rigging and pyrotechnics, turf management, and medical staffing. Captures service order number, service type, requested start/end datetime, venue or event reference, assigned vendor, crew size requirement, estimated vs actual cost, completion status, quality sign-off authority, safety incident flag, and post-service evaluation score. Distinct from purchase orders (goods procurement) — service orders govern labor and service delivery workflows for live event operations with strict event-day deadlines.' .

ind:VendorIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational incidents and non-conformance events attributed to vendor performance failures — including broadcast outages, venue service disruptions, merchandise quality defects, and security breaches. Captures incident date, incident type, severity level, affected event or venue, financial impact estimate, root cause classification, corrective action required, resolution date, and SLA breach linkage. Feeds vendor scorecard deductions and contract penalty calculations.' .

ind:VendorCertification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Certification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Compliance certifications and accreditations held by vendors required for engagement with Sports Entertainment. Captures certification type (ISO 9001, PCI-DSS, WADA compliance, OSHA safety, ADA accessibility, GDPR data processing, diversity certification), issuing body, certification number, issue date, expiry date, renewal reminder flag, and verification status. Ensures vendors meet regulatory and contractual compliance requirements before and during engagement.' .

ind:SkuCatalog rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Sku Catalog' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master product catalog for all official merchandise SKUs including team apparel, memorabilia, accessories, and licensed goods. Serves as the SSOT for product identity, descriptions, brand classifications, league/team associations, and product lifecycle status across all sales channels (Shopify Plus, POS, third-party retail). Tracks SKU codes, product names, categories, sizes, colors, materials, MSRP, and licensing requirements.' .

ind:InventoryPosition rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Inventory Position' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Real-time inventory management record tracking on-hand stock quantities, reserved quantities, available-to-sell units, and stock movement history for each SKU across all storage locations — venue stores, warehouse fulfillment centers, and third-party retail consignment. Captures current position (reorder points, safety stock levels, inventory valuation per location) and transfer activity (origin, destination, quantities moved, transfer reason such as rebalancing or event-day stocking, transfer status, completion date). Sourced from Shopify Plus inventory sync, POS systems, and warehouse management. Supports omnichannel inventory optimization, event-day venue stocking, and inventory reconciliation.' .

ind:RetailLocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Retail Location' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all physical and virtual retail points-of-presence selling official merchandise — venue flagship stores, arena kiosks, warehouse outlets, pop-up event shops, and online storefronts (Shopify Plus). Tracks location name, type (venue store, kiosk, e-commerce, pop-up, third-party), address, operating hours, POS terminal assignments, associated venue, default currency, supported payment methods, and active status. Serves as the SSOT for retail channel geography and storefront configuration across all merchandise sales channels.' .

ind:MerchOrder rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Merch Order' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified transactional record of any merchandise purchase across all channels — Shopify Plus e-commerce, venue POS (arena stores, kiosks, pop-ups), and third-party wholesale. Captures order header (date, channel type, status, total amount, currency, tax, shipping method, fulfillment status) and line-level detail (SKU, quantity, unit price, line discount, line total, line fulfillment status, return eligibility). Channel-specific metadata includes POS terminal ID, cashier ID, payment tender type for in-venue sales; cart session and shipping address for e-commerce; and wholesale account reference for B2B orders. Supports unified omnichannel sales reporting, revenue attribution at SKU level, and PCI-DSS compliant payment data handling. Single source of truth for \'a sale happened\' regardless of channel.' .

ind:OrderLine rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Order Line' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual line item within a merchandise order representing a single SKU quantity purchased. Captures SKU reference, quantity ordered, unit price, line-level discount, line total, fulfillment status, and return eligibility. Supports revenue attribution at the product level and enables SKU-level sales performance tracking across channels.' .

ind:LicensingAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Licensing Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for IP licensing agreements with manufacturers, brand partners, and third-party retailers authorizing production and sale of officially licensed merchandise. Captures licensor, licensee, licensed IP (team name, logo, player NIL rights), product categories covered, royalty rate, minimum guaranteed royalty, territory, agreement start/end dates, exclusivity terms, and compliance audit requirements. Supports NIL (Name Image and Likeness) tracking for athlete-branded merchandise.' .

ind:RoyaltyPayment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Royalty Payment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of royalty calculations, periodic reporting submissions, and disbursements to IP rights holders (leagues, teams, athletes, player associations) based on licensed merchandise sales. Captures reporting period, gross sales by category/territory/channel, applicable royalty rate, calculated royalty due, adjustments, deductions, net royalty paid, payment date, payment status, report submission date, report status (draft, submitted, accepted, disputed), and licensor acceptance. Supports CBA and NIL compliance reporting, licensor audit rights, financial reconciliation of IP revenue sharing, and licensing agreement reporting obligations.' .

ind:MerchandiseGoodsReceipt rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Merchandise Goods Receipt' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record confirming physical receipt of merchandise inventory from a supplier against a purchase order. Captures receipt date, warehouse location, received quantities per SKU, condition on arrival (acceptable, damaged, short-shipped), quality inspection status, and discrepancies versus PO quantities. Triggers inventory position updates and initiates supplier discrepancy resolution workflows.' .

ind:FulfillmentShipment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Fulfillment Shipment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Outbound shipment record for merchandise orders fulfilled from warehouse or venue store to end customer. Captures carrier name, tracking number, ship date, estimated delivery date, actual delivery date, shipment status, shipping cost, package dimensions/weight, and origin location. Supports DTC e-commerce fulfillment SLA tracking and fan delivery experience management via Shopify Plus fulfillment workflows.' .

ind:ReturnRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Return Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Customer merchandise return and exchange request record capturing the reason for return, original order reference, items being returned, return authorization number, return method (mail-in, in-store), refund or exchange preference, refund amount, and resolution status. Supports omnichannel returns policy enforcement and reverse logistics tracking for both Shopify Plus and POS channels.' .

ind:PriceList rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Price List' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified pricing and promotions configuration defining all price points and discount offers for merchandise SKUs across channels and customer segments. Captures base pricing (MSRP, wholesale, VIP member tiers), effective date ranges, channel applicability, and currency. Also owns promotional campaigns — percentage discounts, BOGO offers, free shipping, bundle deals, promo codes, usage limits, redemption counts, and event-day or championship launch pricing events. Supports dynamic pricing, fan loyalty reward redemptions, and promotional campaign performance tracking.' .

ind:Promotion rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Promotion' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Promotional campaign record defining discount offers, bundle deals, and limited-time pricing events for merchandise. Captures promotion name, type (percentage discount, BOGO, free shipping, bundle), applicable SKUs or categories, discount value, promo code, start/end dates, channel restrictions, usage limits, and redemption count. Supports event-day promotions, championship merchandise launches, and fan loyalty reward redemptions.' .

ind:ComplianceCheck rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Compliance Check' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Quality and brand compliance inspection record for licensed merchandise verifying adherence to league and team brand standards, logo usage guidelines, color specifications, material quality, and IP protection requirements. Captures inspection date, SKU inspected, compliance checklist results, pass/fail status per criterion, violations identified, corrective action required, inspector identity, resolution deadline, and final compliance status. Supports IP protection obligations under licensing agreements, league brand governance, and counterfeit prevention programs.' .

ind:Supplier rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Supplier' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for merchandise suppliers, manufacturers, and contract producers who supply official licensed goods. Captures supplier name, type (manufacturer, distributor, print-on-demand), country of origin, contact details, payment terms, lead time, quality rating, certifications (ethical sourcing, ISO), and active status. Distinct from the partner domain\'s broader vendor registry — this is the merchandise-specific supplier master for procurement and quality management.' .

ind:InventoryTransfer rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Inventory Transfer' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record of merchandise stock movements between retail locations, warehouses, and fulfillment centers. Captures transfer request date, origin location, destination location, SKUs and quantities transferred, transfer reason (rebalancing, event-day stocking, store closure), transfer status, and actual completion date. Supports omnichannel inventory optimization and event-day venue store stocking workflows.' .

ind:WholesaleAccount rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Wholesale Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for wholesale and third-party retail accounts authorized to sell official licensed merchandise — sporting goods chains, department stores, airport retailers, and online marketplaces. Captures account name, type, territory, authorized product categories, wholesale pricing tier, minimum order quantities, account status, and periodic sell-through reporting (units sold by SKU, sell-through rates, ending inventory on hand, report submission dates). Serves as the single source of truth for B2B retail partner identity, authorization, performance tracking, and sell-through data that feeds royalty calculations and inventory replenishment decisions.' .

ind:MemorabiliaItem rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Memorabilia Item' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for authenticated sports memorabilia items — autographed jerseys, game-used equipment, championship rings, and collectibles. Captures item name, athlete association, authentication certificate number, authentication provider, game or event provenance, condition grade, edition size (limited/open), acquisition cost, and current valuation. Distinct from standard SKU catalog items due to unique authentication, provenance tracking, and collectible valuation requirements.' .

ind:MediaRightsDeal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Media Rights Deal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of media rights agreements with broadcast partners (RSN, OTT, linear TV networks), including granular rights window definitions. Captures rights holder, territory, sport/league, exclusivity type, deal value, contract term, revenue share structure, rights categories (live, replay, highlights, PPV), and per-window platform/territory/time-period entitlements with sublicensing permissions. SSOT for all broadcast rights ownership, licensing terms, and rights window enforcement. Sourced from Dalet Galaxy and Salesforce CRM.' .

ind:BroadcastSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational schedule of all planned and confirmed broadcast windows across linear TV, OTT, IPTV, and RSN platforms. Tracks event-to-channel assignments, air time, time zone, blackout applicability, feed type (live, tape-delay, replay), and production assignments. Core operational backbone for broadcast distribution — every broadcast begins as a schedule entry. Sourced from Dalet Galaxy broadcast workflow.' .

ind:Channel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Channel' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all broadcast channels and distribution outlets managed by Sports Entertainment — including RSN affiliates, OTT streaming channels, IPTV feeds, linear TV networks, and DTC streaming services. Captures channel name, type (linear/OTT/IPTV/DTC), platform operator, geographic coverage, language, resolution tier (SD/HD/4K), and active status.' .

ind:BlackoutRule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Blackout Rule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Business rules governing broadcast blackouts by territory, event, channel, and rights agreement. Captures blackout type (local, national, international), triggering conditions (ticket sales threshold, RSN exclusivity, league mandate), effective date range, override eligibility, and enforcement mechanism. Critical for rights compliance and RSN exclusivity protection. Sourced from league governance and media rights deal terms.' .

ind:BroadcastDrmPolicy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Drm Policy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Digital Rights Management policy definitions governing content protection, encryption standards, device authentication, and playback restrictions for OTT, IPTV, and DTC streaming platforms. Captures DRM technology (Widevine, FairPlay, PlayReady), content tier, geo-restriction rules, concurrent stream limits, download permissions, and watermarking requirements. Ensures IP protection and rights compliance.' .

ind:LiveFeed rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Live Feed' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record of each live broadcast feed produced and distributed for a scheduled event. Captures source venue, OB (Outside Broadcast) unit assignment, signal type (satellite, fiber, IP), encoding format (H.264/H.265), resolution (SD/HD/4K/8K), audio tracks, commentary language, feed status (active, standby, failed, backup), CDN origin endpoint, and redundancy configuration. Core operational entity for live broadcast production, distribution monitoring, and failover management.' .

ind:PpvPackage rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Ppv Package' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of Pay-Per-View event packages and transactional record of PPV purchases. Captures PPV event name, associated event, pricing tiers (consumer, wholesale, international), distribution window, platform availability, bundling options, revenue share terms, and purchase eligibility rules. For transactions: buyer reference, purchase timestamp, platform, payment method, price, currency, promotional discount, access token, and fulfillment status. SSOT for PPV product definitions, commercial packaging, and purchase revenue. Integrates with PCI-DSS compliant payment processing.' .

ind:PpvTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Ppv Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of individual PPV purchases by consumers or wholesale distributors. Captures buyer reference, PPV package, purchase timestamp, platform (OTT, IPTV, cable), payment method, purchase price, currency, promotional discount applied, access token issued, and fulfillment status. Core revenue transaction for PPV monetization. Integrates with PCI-DSS compliant payment processing.' .

ind:StreamingSubscription rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Streaming Subscription' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of fan streaming subscriptions to DTC and OTT broadcast services. Captures subscriber reference, subscription plan tier (basic, premium, all-access), billing cycle, start/end dates, platform (mobile, web, connected TV), auto-renewal flag, promotional rate, and current status. SSOT for streaming subscription lifecycle within the broadcast domain. Complements fan domain identity records.' .

ind:MediaAsset rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Media Asset' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of broadcast media assets managed within the Dalet Galaxy DAM system. Captures asset ID, title, asset type (live recording, highlight reel, replay, promo, interstitial), format, duration, resolution, language, sport/league association, event association, rights clearance status, archive location, and metadata tags. SSOT for broadcast-owned media asset inventory distinct from content domain editorial assets.' .

ind:BroadcastRightsWindow rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Rights Window' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Granular rights window records derived from media rights deals, defining the specific time periods, platforms, and territories in which a rights holder may broadcast specific content. Captures rights deal reference, content category, platform type, territory, window start/end, exclusivity flag, sublicensing permission, and rights fee allocation. Enables precise rights enforcement at the content-platform-territory level.' .

ind:Production rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Production' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record of each broadcast production instance for a scheduled event, including crew and commentary team assignments. Captures production type (live, studio, remote OB), director, technical producer, production company, equipment manifest, venue technical setup, graphics package version, pre-show/post-show segments, production status, and commentary team composition (play-by-play, color analyst, sideline reporter) with language and market designations. Links broadcast schedule to physical production execution. Sourced from Dalet Galaxy broadcast workflow.' .

ind:RightsViolation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Violation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record of detected or reported media rights violations including unauthorized rebroadcasts, geo-restriction breaches, DRM circumvention, blackout non-compliance, and unauthorized clip usage on social platforms. Captures violation type, detection method (automated/manual/third-party), detected datetime, platform, territory, infringing party, evidence reference (screenshots, stream captures), enforcement action taken (DMCA takedown, cease-and-desist, financial penalty), resolution status, and legal case reference. Supports rights protection, legal compliance workflows, and rights deal enforcement reporting.' .

ind:AudienceRating rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Audience Rating' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of broadcast audience measurement data per scheduled broadcast window. Captures channel, territory, measurement source (Nielsen, BARB, OzTAM, Comscore, internal streaming analytics), rating type (GRP, CPM, reach, frequency, viewership), total viewers, demographic breakdown (age, gender, income), peak concurrent viewers, average minute audience (AMA), share percentage, and time-shifted viewing. Operational data used for rights valuation, advertiser rate card justification, scheduling optimization, and contractual audience guarantee reconciliation.' .

ind:BroadcastAdInventory rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Ad Inventory' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog and transactional record of advertising inventory slots and their placements within broadcast windows across linear TV, OTT, and streaming platforms. Captures slot type (pre-roll, mid-roll, billboard, in-break), duration, broadcast schedule reference, channel, territory, CPM floor rate, sold status, sponsorship exclusivity flag, and for executed placements: advertiser, creative asset, placement datetime, actual CPM achieved, impressions delivered, and trafficking confirmation. SSOT for broadcast advertising inventory management and placement execution. Distinct from sponsorship domain brand activations.' .

ind:AdPlacement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Ad Placement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each advertising placement executed within a broadcast window. Captures ad inventory slot reference, advertiser, creative asset, placement datetime, actual CPM achieved, impressions delivered, platform, territory, and trafficking confirmation. Core revenue transaction for broadcast advertising monetization. Integrates with sponsorship domain for brand-level reporting.' .

ind:SublicenseAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Sublicense Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of sublicensing arrangements where Sports Entertainment grants secondary broadcast rights to third-party distributors, RSN affiliates, or international broadcasters derived from primary media rights deals. Captures parent rights deal, sublicensee, territory, content scope, sublicense fee, revenue share, term, and compliance obligations. Distinct from the primary media_rights_deal as it represents a downstream rights grant.' .

ind:RightsRoyalty rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Royalty' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of royalty and rights fee payments due or received under media rights deals and sublicense agreements. Captures rights deal or sublicense reference, payment period, calculated royalty amount, currency, payment due date, payment received date, and reconciliation status. Core financial transaction for broadcast rights revenue recognition and partner settlement. Feeds finance domain general ledger.' .

ind:Employee rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Employee' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SSOT master record for all workforce members across Sports Entertainment — full-time staff, part-time event crew, broadcast crews, league officials, and seasonal workers. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors HCM. Captures legal name, employment type, hire date, termination date, job classification, cost center assignment, work location, employment status, FLSA classification, union membership flag, CBA agreement reference, and identity verification status. This is the authoritative workforce identity record referenced by all HR sub-domains.' .

ind:Position rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Position' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Organizational position master defining approved headcount slots and job classification within the Sports Entertainment org structure. Captures position title, job code, job family (Event Operations, Broadcast Production, Athlete Services, Venue Management), job level, FLSA status (exempt/non-exempt), EEO-1 category, pay grade band, department, reporting line, FTE allocation, position type (permanent, seasonal, event-day), budget approval status, open/filled status, union eligibility flag, and CBA applicability. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Position Management and Job Catalog. Enables workforce planning, headcount governance, compensation banding, compliance reporting, and workforce segmentation across leagues, venues, broadcast, and corporate functions.' .

ind:OrgUnit rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Org Unit' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Organizational hierarchy master representing departments, divisions, leagues, venues, and broadcast units within Sports Entertainment. Captures org unit name, org unit type (department, division, league, venue, broadcast network), parent org unit, cost center code, effective date, and active status. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Org Chart. Provides the structural backbone for workforce reporting, budget allocation, and span-of-control analysis.' .

ind:JobApplication rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Job Application' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Talent acquisition lifecycle record managing the end-to-end hiring process at Sports Entertainment — from headcount requisition approval through candidate offer acceptance. Captures requisition management (position linked, hiring manager, recruiter assigned, requisition status, target start date, sourcing channels, internal/external posting, time-to-fill), candidate pipeline (applicant identity, source channel, application status, interview stage, assessment scores, background check status, offer details), and hiring analytics (funnel conversion rates, source effectiveness, DEI hiring metrics, cost-per-hire). Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Recruiting Management. SSOT for all talent acquisition activity including requisition governance and candidate lifecycle.' .

ind:EmploymentContract rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Employment Contract' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Formal employment agreement and compensation terms record for each workforce member at Sports Entertainment, including full-time staff, seasonal event crew, broadcast talent, and league officials. Captures contract terms (contract type — permanent, fixed-term, seasonal, zero-hours; start/end date, contracted hours, probation period, contract status), compensation structure (base pay rate, pay frequency, salary range min/mid/max, bonus target percentage, commission eligibility, merit increase schedule, NIL-related compensation provisions for athlete-adjacent roles), CBA provisions (CBA agreement reference, union local), and effective dates. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central and Compensation Management. Supports CBA compliance, labor cost forecasting, pay equity analysis, annual compensation review cycles, and workforce planning.' .

ind:PayrollRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Payroll Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Payroll processing record capturing each pay run result for an employee at Sports Entertainment. Includes pay period start/end, gross pay, net pay, federal/state/local tax withholdings, FICA contributions, union dues deducted, overtime hours and premium pay, shift differentials (event-day, broadcast, overnight), garnishments, direct deposit status, and payroll run date. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Payroll. SSOT for all compensation disbursement data and payroll audit compliance.' .

ind:BenefitEnrollment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Benefit Enrollment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee benefits enrollment record capturing elected benefit plans for each workforce member at Sports Entertainment. Tracks benefit plan type (medical, dental, vision, 401k, life insurance, disability, FSA, HSA, EAP), coverage tier (employee only, employee+spouse, family), enrollment effective date, annual election amount, employer contribution, employee contribution, and open enrollment period. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Benefits. Supports benefits cost reporting, ACA compliance, and total rewards analysis.' .

ind:LeaveRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Leave Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee leave and absence request record managing all time-off events at Sports Entertainment. Captures leave type (FMLA, PTO, sick, bereavement, jury duty, military, parental, event-day comp time), request date, leave start date, leave end date, approved hours/days, approval status, approving manager, FMLA eligibility flag, intermittent leave flag, and return-to-work date. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Time and Attendance. Supports FMLA compliance, absence trend analysis, and event staffing gap identification.' .

ind:ShiftAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Shift Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Workforce time and attendance record capturing both scheduled shifts and actual hours worked at Sports Entertainment events, venues, and broadcast operations. For scheduling: shift date, start/end time, shift type (event-day, broadcast, venue operations, office, overnight), assigned location, role during shift, scheduled hours. For time reporting: actual hours worked, regular/overtime/double-time breakdown, event-day premium hours, on-call hours, travel time, break deductions. Workflow: timesheet submission date, manager approval status, payroll processing status, overtime flag, no-show flag. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Time and Attendance. Feeds directly into payroll processing and supports CBA overtime compliance, FLSA audit trails, OSHA hours-of-service compliance, and event staffing labor cost tracking.' .

ind:PerformanceReview rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Performance Review' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee performance evaluation and talent succession record capturing formal review cycles and leadership pipeline planning at Sports Entertainment. For performance: tracks review period, review type (annual, mid-year, probationary, event-season), overall rating, competency ratings, goal achievement, manager comments, self-assessment, calibration status, PIP flag, promotion recommendation. For succession: captures target position for succession, readiness tier (ready now, 1-2 years, 3+ years), nominated successor, development gap assessment, retention risk rating. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Performance & Goals and Succession & Development. Drives merit increase decisions, succession planning, talent pipeline management, and critical role coverage.' .

ind:LearningEnrollment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Learning Enrollment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee training, development, and credential management record at Sports Entertainment. Covers learning activities: course/program name, learning type (mandatory compliance, CBA-required safety, broadcast certification, leadership development, OSHA certification), enrollment/completion dates, pass/fail status, training hours, delivery method, cost. Covers credentials: credential type (OSHA 10/30, first aid/CPR, broadcast engineering license, food handler permit, security license, forklift certification), issuing authority, issue/expiration dates, renewal status, verification status. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Learning Management System. SSOT for all workforce competency, certification, and compliance training data. Supports OSHA compliance tracking, CBA training obligations, venue access control, and broadcast regulatory licensing.' .

ind:OshaIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Osha Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'OSHA workplace safety incident record capturing all recordable and reportable safety events at Sports Entertainment venues, broadcast sites, and office locations. Tracks incident date, incident type (injury, illness, near-miss, fatality), OSHA recordability classification (300 log, 300A summary), injured employee, incident location, event association (if event-day incident), body part affected, nature of injury, days away from work, restricted duty days, root cause, corrective action taken, and OSHA reporting submission date. Supports OSHA 300/300A compliance and venue safety program management.' .

ind:EmployeeCertification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Employee Certification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee credential and certification master tracking all professional licenses, safety certifications, and access credentials held by Sports Entertainment workforce members. Captures credential type (OSHA 10/30, first aid/CPR, broadcast engineering license, food handler permit, security license, forklift certification, event management certification), issuing authority, issue date, expiration date, renewal status, and verification status. Supports OSHA compliance, venue access control, and broadcast regulatory licensing requirements.' .

ind:LaborRelationsCase rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Labor Relations Case' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Labor relations case record documenting all formal employee relations actions at Sports Entertainment including grievances, arbitrations, and CBA-related disputes. References league.cba_agreement for league-level CBAs.' .

ind:EmploymentEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Employment Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Employee lifecycle movement record capturing all organizational transitions and separations at Sports Entertainment. For internal movements: tracks movement type (lateral transfer, promotion, demotion, temporary assignment, inter-league secondment, venue-to-venue transfer), from/to position, from/to org unit, compensation change flag. For separations: tracks separation type (voluntary resignation, involuntary termination, retirement, end of seasonal contract), exit interview data, equipment return, system access revocation, rehire eligibility. Common fields: effective date, reason code, initiating manager, HR approval status. Sourced from SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central. Supports internal mobility reporting, turnover analysis, and org change management.' .

ind:FanProfile rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Profile' ;
    rdfs:comment 'SSOT master identity record for every individual fan across all engagement channels. Captures core demographic data (name, DOB, gender, nationality), contact details, preferred language, communication preferences, accessibility requirements, and account status. Sourced from Salesforce CRM and Adobe Experience Platform. Serves B2C individual fans, family account holders, season ticket holders, VIP members, and fan club members. This is the golden record for fan identity — all other fan domain entities reference this via fan_profile_id.' .

ind:Account rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational account record linking a fan profile to their registered digital or venue account. Tracks account type (individual, family, corporate group), account status, registration channel (web, mobile, in-venue kiosk), login credentials metadata, account tier, and tokenized payment methods on file (card brand, last four digits, expiry, default flag, PCI-DSS token). Distinct from fan_profile (identity) — this is the transactional account used for purchases, ticketing, loyalty redemptions, and stored payment instruments. Sourced from Salesforce CRM Account object.' .

ind:Household rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Household' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Groups individual fan profiles into a household or family unit for B2C relationship management. Tracks household name, primary account holder reference, number of members, household address, combined lifetime value, household income band, and household segment classification. Enables family ticket packages, household-level NPS tracking, multi-member loyalty aggregation, and season ticket holder family accounts. Critical for direct mail deduplication and household-level spend analysis.' .

ind:LoyaltyProgram rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Loyalty Program' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master definition of each fan loyalty program offered across leagues, venues, and digital platforms. Captures program name, program type (points-based, tier-based, hybrid), earning rules summary, redemption rules summary, program currency name (e.g., \'Fan Points\', \'Arena Credits\'), program status, effective dates, and associated league or venue scope. Reference entity that governs all loyalty enrollment and transaction records.' .

ind:LoyaltyEnrollment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Loyalty Enrollment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Records a fan\'s active enrollment in a specific loyalty program. Tracks enrollment date, current tier (e.g., Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum), tier qualification date, tier expiry date, cumulative points earned lifetime, current redeemable points balance, points expiry date, enrollment channel, and enrollment status. One fan may be enrolled in multiple programs. Sourced from Salesforce CRM and Adobe Experience Platform loyalty modules.' .

ind:LoyaltyTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Loyalty Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional ledger of all loyalty point earning and redemption events for a fan. Captures transaction type (earn, redeem, adjust, expire, transfer), points amount, transaction date, triggering activity (ticket purchase, merchandise buy, check-in, content view, referral), reference order or event ID, running balance after transaction, and transaction status. Provides full audit trail for loyalty currency movements per fan enrollment.' .

ind:Membership rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Membership' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for a fan\'s paid or complimentary membership and its associated benefits. Tracks membership type (season ticket holder, VIP club, fan club, OTT subscription), membership number, start/end dates, renewal status, auto-renew flag, fee, payment frequency, assigned seat block, and membership status. Also defines attached benefits: benefit type (priority ticketing, parking pass, merchandise discount, VIP lounge access, meet-and-greet, exclusive content), quantity/usage limits, redemption method, benefit value, and validity period. Distinct from loyalty enrollment — membership is a paid contractual relationship with defined benefit packages, not a points program.' .

ind:MembershipBenefit rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Membership Benefit' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines the specific benefits attached to a membership tier or individual membership record. Captures benefit type (priority ticketing, parking pass, merchandise discount, VIP lounge access, meet-and-greet, exclusive content access), benefit description, quantity or usage limit, redemption method, benefit value, and validity period. Enables benefit fulfillment tracking and VIP experience management across venues and events.' .

ind:Segment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Segment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'CRM segmentation records classifying fans into behavioral, demographic, and value-based segments for targeted marketing and personalization. Captures segment name, segment type (RFM, behavioral, demographic, psychographic, predictive), definition criteria, segment size, creation date, last refresh date, and owning campaign or business unit. Sourced from Adobe Experience Platform audience segments and Salesforce CRM campaigns. Enables personalized fan engagement, DTC marketing, and campaign targeting.' .

ind:SegmentAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Segment Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association table recording which fans belong to which CRM segments at a given point in time. Tracks fan profile ID, segment ID, assignment date, assignment method (rule-based, manual, ML-predicted), assignment score or confidence, expiry date, and active flag. Supports time-variant segment membership for campaign targeting, personalization, and NPS cohort analysis. Carries its own business data (assignment method, score) beyond a simple M:N link.' .

ind:ConsentPreference rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Consent Preference' ;
    rdfs:comment 'GDPR and CCPA compliance record capturing each fan\'s data privacy consent and communication preferences. Tracks consent type (marketing email, SMS, push notification, data sharing with partners, profiling/personalization, cookie consent), consent status (granted, withdrawn, pending), consent date, withdrawal date, consent source (web form, mobile app, in-venue kiosk, call center), jurisdiction (EU-GDPR, CA-CCPA, UK-GDPR), and consent version. SSOT for all fan privacy obligations.' .

ind:NpsSurvey rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Nps Survey' ;
    rdfs:comment 'NPS (Net Promoter Score) survey program and response records. Captures survey campaign details: survey name, type (post-event, post-purchase, seasonal, relationship), associated event or touchpoint, channel (email, in-app, SMS, in-venue kiosk), open/close dates, target segment, and response rate. Also captures individual fan responses: NPS score (0-10), promoter/passive/detractor classification, verbatim comment text, response timestamp, follow-up action flag, and associated event or purchase reference. SSOT for fan satisfaction measurement. Feeds CRM case management for detractor recovery workflows.' .

ind:NpsResponse rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Nps Response' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual fan NPS survey response record. Captures fan profile ID, survey ID, NPS score (0-10), promoter/passive/detractor classification, verbatim comment text, response channel, response timestamp, follow-up action flag, follow-up status, and associated event or purchase reference. SSOT for fan satisfaction measurement. Feeds CRM case management for detractor recovery workflows.' .

ind:EngagementEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Engagement Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'High-volume transactional record of every discrete fan engagement interaction across all channels — event attendance check-in, app session, content view, social share, merchandise browse, loyalty redemption, live stream watch, in-venue beacon detection, contest entry, and content follow/watchlist actions. Captures engagement type, channel (mobile app, web, in-venue, broadcast, social), timestamp, duration, associated event or content ID, device type, location context, and engagement value score. Sourced from Adobe Experience Platform behavioral data stream. Primary feed for RFM scoring, personalization models, and fan lifetime value calculation.' .

ind:Communication rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Communication' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of every outbound communication sent to a fan across all channels (email, SMS, push notification, direct mail, in-app message). Captures communication type, campaign or trigger name, channel, send timestamp, delivery status, open timestamp, click timestamp, opt-out flag, and associated segment or journey. Sourced from Salesforce CRM and Adobe Experience Platform campaign execution logs. Enables communication fatigue management and GDPR suppression compliance.' .

ind:ServiceCase rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Service Case' ;
    rdfs:comment 'CRM service case record for fan support interactions — ticketing disputes, membership billing issues, lost-and-found, accessibility accommodation requests, complaint escalations, and VIP concierge requests. Captures case type, case subject, description, priority, status, open date, resolution date, resolution notes, assigned agent, channel of origin (phone, email, chat, social, in-venue), and associated fan account. Sourced from Salesforce CRM Case object.' .

ind:PaymentMethod rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Payment Method' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Tokenized payment instrument records stored on file for a fan account. Captures payment method type (credit card, debit card, digital wallet, direct debit, gift card), card brand, last four digits, expiry month/year, billing address reference, tokenization provider, token value, default payment flag, and PCI-DSS compliance status. Enables one-click ticket purchases, auto-renewal of memberships, and merchandise checkout. Compliant with PCI-DSS tokenization standards.' .

ind:Club rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Club' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for official fan clubs and their membership enrollments. Captures fan club name, associated team or athlete, club type (official, supporters trust, regional chapter), founding date, membership fee structure, club status, geographic territory, and club administrator contact. Also tracks individual member enrollments: membership number, join date, renewal date, membership tier within the club, dues payment status, voting rights, and chapter assignment. Enables fan club community participation, event access privileges, and engagement programs.' .

ind:ClubMembership rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Club Membership' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association record linking a fan profile to a specific fan club with membership details. Captures membership number, join date, renewal date, membership status, membership tier within the club, dues payment status, voting rights flag, and chapter assignment. Distinct from the broader loyalty enrollment or venue membership — this specifically governs fan club community participation and associated privileges.' .

ind:RegulatoryFiling rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Regulatory Filing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all regulatory submissions made to governing bodies including FIFA, IOC, NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, FCC, SEC, WADA, and CAS. Tracks filing type, submission date, governing body (FK to governing_body), jurisdiction, filing status, due date, submitted by, acknowledgment reference, and linked compliance obligation (FK to obligation). Serves as the authoritative register of all formal regulatory submissions and enables deadline tracking and overdue alerting.' .

ind:GoverningBody rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Governing Body' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference master for all sports and entertainment governing bodies and regulatory authorities that Sports Entertainment must comply with — FIFA, IOC, NFL League Office, NBA League Office, WADA, CAS, FCC, SEC, OSHA, ADA, GDPR supervisory authorities, PCI SSC, SOX auditors, ISO 20121 certifiers. Captures body name, acronym, jurisdiction, regulatory domain, contact authority, and applicable frameworks.' .

ind:Obligation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Obligation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all compliance obligations imposed on Sports Entertainment by governing bodies, regulations, and internal policies. Each obligation record captures the regulatory framework (GDPR, CCPA, PCI-DSS, WADA, ADA, SOX, OSHA, CBA), obligation type, effective date, expiry date, responsible business unit, enforcement consequence, review frequency, and linked governing body. Acts as the SSOT for what the organization is required to do.' .

ind:Policy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Policy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all internal compliance policies and codes of conduct enforced across Sports Entertainment — data privacy policies (GDPR/CCPA), anti-doping policies (WADA), payment security policies (PCI-DSS), venue accessibility policies (ADA), broadcast content policies (FCC), anti-corruption policies, and CBA-mandated conduct rules. Captures policy name, version, effective date, owner, approval authority, review cycle, and linked regulatory obligation.' .

ind:AuditSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Audit Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Planned audit calendar for all compliance audits across Sports Entertainment — PCI-DSS QSA audits, SOX internal controls, OSHA venue safety inspections, ADA accessibility audits, GDPR data protection audits, WADA program audits, and ISO 20121 sustainability audits. Captures audit type, scheduled date, auditor assignment (internal/external), scope definition, target business unit, venue or system in scope, audit cycle frequency, and linked compliance obligation. Enables compliance teams to manage the forward-looking audit pipeline and identify scheduling conflicts.' .

ind:AuditEngagement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Audit Engagement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Complete audit lifecycle record from planning through execution and disposition for all compliance audits — PCI-DSS QSA audits, SOX internal controls, OSHA venue safety inspections, ADA accessibility audits, GDPR data protection audits, WADA program audits, and ISO 20121 sustainability audits. Captures planned audit details (audit type, scheduled date, auditor assignment, scope, target business unit, venue/system in scope, cycle frequency, linked obligation) and execution details (actual start/end dates, lead auditor, audit firm, findings count, overall opinion, report issuance date, management response due date, final disposition). Status progression from scheduled through in-progress to completed enables both forward-looking audit pipeline management and historical audit trail.' .

ind:AuditFinding rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Audit Finding' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual finding or observation raised during a compliance audit engagement. Captures finding reference, linked audit engagement, finding category (critical/major/minor/observation), regulatory framework implicated, description of non-conformance, root cause, recommended remediation, assigned owner, target remediation date, and finding status (open/in-remediation/closed/accepted-risk). Supports PCI-DSS, SOX, OSHA, ADA, and GDPR audit trails.' .

ind:DopingTest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Doping Test' ;
    rdfs:comment 'WADA anti-doping program operational record encompassing both testing events and athlete whereabouts filings. For tests: captures test reference number, athlete identifier, test type (in-competition/out-of-competition), sample type (urine/blood/ABP), collection date, collection location, DCO identifier, laboratory reference, chain of custody status, result status (negative/adverse/atypical/pending), and WADA ADAMS reference. For whereabouts: captures filing period (quarter), submission date, overnight location, training and competition schedule, filing compliance status (compliant/missed/incomplete), and missed filing count toward Article 2.4 violation threshold. Core operational record for the complete anti-doping program lifecycle from whereabouts compliance through sample collection and result management.' .

ind:DopingViolation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Doping Violation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Record of an Anti-Doping Rule Violation (ADRV) issued against an athlete following an adverse or atypical analytical finding or non-analytical violation (whereabouts failure, tampering, refusal). Captures violation type, linked doping test, notification date, provisional suspension date, hearing date, sanction imposed (ban duration), appeal status, CAS arbitration reference if appealed, and reinstatement eligibility date. Governed by WADA Code and CAS jurisprudence.' .

ind:WhereaboutsFiling rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Whereabouts Filing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'WADA whereabouts information filing submitted by registered testing pool athletes. Captures athlete identifier, filing period (quarter), submission date, submission method (ADAMS portal), overnight location, training schedule, competition schedule, and filing compliance status (compliant/missed/incomplete). Three missed filings within 12 months constitute a whereabouts failure violation under WADA Code Article 2.4.' .

ind:EligibilityCertification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Eligibility Certification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified eligibility, certification, and exemption record confirming or modifying compliance status for athletes, participants, venues, and events. For certifications: covers league eligibility, amateur status, age/nationality eligibility, anti-doping clearance, medical clearance, ADA venue accessibility certification, and event safety certification. For exemptions: covers Therapeutic Use Exemptions (TUEs per WADA Code Article 4.4), broadcast territorial exemptions, ADA undue hardship exemptions, and FCC content exemptions. Captures record type (certification/exemption), issuing or reviewing authority, certified/exempt entity, effective and expiry dates, status, conditions or restrictions, medical justification (for TUEs), approved substance/method, WADA ADAMS TUE reference, and accommodation requirements. Integrates with athlete domain for competition gating and venue domain for operational permits.' .

ind:ArbitrationCase rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Arbitration Case' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified dispute resolution and case management record for all legal proceedings — CAS (Court of Arbitration for Sport) arbitration, internal arbitration, civil litigation, regulatory investigations, criminal referrals, IP infringement, employment disputes, and CBA grievances. Captures case reference, case type and jurisdiction (sports arbitration vs civil court vs regulatory), claimant/respondent or plaintiff/defendant, filing date, panel or judge composition, external counsel, hearing and trial dates, interim measures, discovery status, estimated liability, award or judgment summary, settlement terms, enforcement status, and matter management reference. Serves as the SSOT for all dispute proceedings regardless of forum.' .

ind:PrivacyRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Privacy Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified data subject interaction record under GDPR, CCPA, and applicable privacy regulations covering both rights requests and consent management. For requests: captures request type (access/SAR, erasure, portability, rectification, restriction, opt-out of sale), requestor identity, submission channel, verification status, regulatory deadline (30-day GDPR / 45-day CCPA), fulfillment date, and response outcome. For consent: captures consent type (marketing, analytics, third-party sharing, cookies, biometric data), consent channel (web, app, in-venue kiosk), consent timestamp, policy version, withdrawal timestamp, and consent proof reference. Provides the single fan-privacy SSOT for all data subject touchpoints and integrates with Adobe Experience Platform consent management.' .

ind:DataProcessingRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Data Processing Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'GDPR Article 30 Record of Processing Activities (RoPA) with integrated Article 35 Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA/PIA) for all personal data processing activities. The authoritative register and risk assessment record capturing processing activity name, controller/processor role, data categories (fan PII, athlete health data, payment data, biometric data), purposes, legal basis, data subjects, retention period, third-party recipients, cross-border transfer mechanisms, security measures, DPIA/PIA assessment type, risk level, identified risks, risk mitigation measures, DPO consultation date, supervisory authority consultation requirement, assessment outcome, approval date, and review schedule. Mandatory for GDPR compliance and required before launching new fan platforms, biometric ticketing, athlete health systems, or any high-risk processing activity.' .

ind:AdaAccommodation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Ada Accommodation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) accommodation request and fulfillment record for fans, athletes, and employees requiring accessibility accommodations at venues and events. Captures requestor type, accommodation type (wheelchair seating, hearing loop, sign language interpreter, accessible parking, service animal area, sensory room), event or venue, request date, fulfillment status, assigned coordinator, and accommodation outcome. Supports ADA Title II/III compliance for venue operations.' .

ind:IncidentReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Incident Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified compliance and safety incident register from detection through notification, remediation, and closure. Captures regulatory breaches, personal data breaches (with GDPR 72-hour supervisory authority notification tracking and data subject notification), OSHA workplace incidents, venue safety incidents, broadcast content violations (FCC), and anti-doping program incidents. Records incident type, date, location, severity, affected parties, regulatory framework implicated, immediate response actions, root cause, corrective actions, breach notification details (notified authority, notification date, categories and volume of affected records, likely consequences, measures taken, GDPR deadline compliance status, notification outcome), and closure status. Serves as the single incident register and breach notification tracker eliminating the need for separate notification records.' .

ind:Sanction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Sanction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified enforcement action and disciplinary sanction record issued by governing bodies or internal compliance authorities against athletes, officials, teams, or the organization. Covers all sanction types including Anti-Doping Rule Violations (ADRVs from adverse/atypical findings and non-analytical violations such as whereabouts failures and tampering), suspensions, fines, points deductions, disqualifications, license revocations, and warnings. Captures sanction type, sanctioned entity, issuing authority, regulatory basis, violation type and details, linked doping test or investigation, notification and provisional suspension dates, hearing date, sanction period, fine amount, WADA ADAMS reference, appeal status and window, CAS arbitration reference, reinstatement eligibility date, and enforcement status. Single Source of Truth for all penalties, violations, and enforcement actions across all governing bodies.' .

ind:Exemption rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Exemption' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Therapeutic Use Exemption (TUE) and regulatory exemption record. Captures exemption type (WADA TUE for prohibited substance/method, broadcast rights territorial exemption, ADA undue hardship exemption, FCC content exemption), applicant, reviewing authority, application date, medical justification (for TUE), approved substance or method, exemption validity period, conditions attached, approval status, and WADA ADAMS TUE reference. Critical for WADA Code Article 4.4 compliance.' .

ind:BreachNotification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Breach Notification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Formal data breach notification record tracking the organization\'s obligations to notify supervisory authorities and affected data subjects following a personal data breach. Captures breach reference, linked incident report, notification type (supervisory authority / data subject), notified authority (e.g., EU DPA, California AG), notification date, breach description, categories and volume of affected records, likely consequences, measures taken, GDPR 72-hour deadline compliance status, and notification outcome.' .

ind:PiaAssessment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Pia Assessment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA) / Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) record conducted for high-risk data processing activities as required by GDPR Article 35. Captures assessment reference, processing activity assessed, assessment type (DPIA/PIA), risk level, identified risks, risk mitigation measures, DPO consultation date, supervisory authority consultation requirement, assessment outcome, approval date, and review schedule. Mandatory for new fan engagement platforms, biometric ticketing, and athlete health data systems.' .

ind:LicensePermit rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'License Permit' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational license and permit register for all licenses and permits required to operate Sports Entertainment venues, events, and broadcasts. Captures license type (venue operating license, broadcast license, liquor license, event permit, gaming license, pyrotechnics permit, FCC broadcast license, music performance license), issuing authority, jurisdiction, license number, issue date, expiry date, renewal status, associated venue or event, and compliance conditions. Distinct from eligibility_certification which covers athlete/participant eligibility.' .

ind:Transcript rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Transcript' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for closed captions, subtitles, and full transcripts associated with video and audio content assets — capturing language, format (SRT, VTT, TTML), generation method (human, AI/ASR), accuracy score, compliance status (ADA/FCC), and sync timing metadata. SSOT for all accessibility text tracks required for OTT, broadcast, and social distribution.' .

ind:StaffPlan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Staff Plan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Event-day staffing plan for a facility specifying required headcount by role (security, medical, ushers, concessions, parking, cleaning, AV/production) for a specific event or event type. Attributes include plan name, event reference, facility reference, role category, required headcount, confirmed headcount, staffing agency reference, shift start/end times, credential requirements, cost estimate, actual cost, and plan approval status. Distinct from workforce domain employee records — this is the venue\'s operational labor demand and fulfillment plan for event execution.' .

ind:TransactionWindow rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Transaction Window' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Defines official league transaction periods (trade deadline, free agency window, waiver period, DFA window, international signing period) with open/close dates, eligible transaction types, franchise participation rules, and penalty provisions for violations. Anchors all roster movement and trade activity to authorized periods. Supports compliance validation for league_trade_transaction and waiver_claim records.' .

ind:Waitlist rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Waitlist' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Queue management record for fans seeking ticket access to sold-out events, season ticket packages, or premium seating upgrades. Captures fan reference, requested product (single event, STH package, suite), priority rank, registration timestamp, queue position, notification preferences, conversion status, and offer expiry. Supports season ticket holder waitlist management (often 5,000+ deep at major franchises), sold-out event demand capture, and premium upgrade queues. Enables demand signaling for dynamic pricing and capacity planning.' .

ind:WeatherContingency rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Weather Contingency' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Weather monitoring and contingency planning records for outdoor events — forecast tracking, delay triggers, cancellation thresholds, dome closure decisions, and fan communication protocols.' .

ind:BroadcastWindow rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Broadcast Window' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association entity linking fixtures to their assigned broadcast windows and production requirements — capturing primary broadcaster, kickoff time constraints driven by broadcast, and territory-specific start times.' .

ind:AttendanceRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Attendance Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Official attendance figures and capacity utilization records for completed events — paid attendance, actual turnstile count, no-shows, comp tickets used, and capacity percentage.' .

ind:Pricing rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Event ;
    rdfs:label 'Pricing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Event-level pricing strategy and tier configuration linking fixture characteristics (rivalry, playoff, day-of-week) to pricing multipliers and dynamic pricing activation rules.' .

ind:ContentRecommendation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Content Recommendation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Platform content recommendation engine output records — recommended content items, recommendation algorithm, confidence score, user context, and engagement outcome tracking.' .

ind:PushNotification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Push Notification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Individual push notification delivery records — message content, target device, delivery status, open/dismiss action, deep link destination, and send trigger (real-time score, breaking news, promotion).' .

ind:AppRelease rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'App Release' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Mobile and web application release management records — version number, release date, platform (iOS/Android/Web), feature changelog, rollout percentage, and crash rate monitoring.' .

ind:SearchQuery rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Platform ;
    rdfs:label 'Search Query' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Fan search query records across platform properties — search term, results returned, result clicked, search context (pre-event, in-venue, content browse), and zero-result flags.' .

ind:VenueManifest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue Manifest' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Venue seating manifest configuration linking ticket inventory to physical seat maps — section/row/seat mapping, ADA locations, obstructed view flags, and kill seats for production equipment.' .

ind:TicketTransfer rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Ticket Transfer' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Peer-to-peer ticket transfer records between fan accounts — capturing sender, recipient, transfer method (mobile, email), transfer timestamp, and terms acceptance.' .

ind:PromoCode rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Promo Code' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Promotional code and discount offer records for ticket purchases — code string, discount type (percentage/fixed/BOGO), validity period, usage limits, and associated campaigns.' .

ind:ParkingPass rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Parking Pass' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Parking pass inventory and sales records associated with event tickets — lot assignment, pass type (general/VIP/tailgate), pricing, and bundling rules with ticket packages.' .

ind:TaxJurisdiction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Tax Jurisdiction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Tax jurisdiction reference data defining applicable tax rates, rules, and filing requirements by geographic location — sales tax, entertainment tax, jock tax, withholding requirements for multi-state athlete compensation.' .

ind:RevenueStream rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Revenue Stream' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Revenue stream classification and tracking master — ticketing, broadcast rights, sponsorship, merchandise, gaming, venue rentals — with budget allocation, growth targets, and seasonal patterns.' .

ind:CashFlowForecast rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Cash Flow Forecast' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Cash flow forecasting records by period and business unit — projected inflows (ticket sales, broadcast payments, sponsorship installments) and outflows (payroll, venue ops, content production) with variance tracking.' .

ind:AuditTrail rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Audit Trail' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Financial transaction audit trail capturing all modifications to journal entries, invoices, and payments — user, timestamp, before/after values, and approval chain for SOX compliance.' .

ind:KpiDefinition rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Kpi Definition' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) defined across Sports Entertainment business units — ticketing revenue per event, broadcast audience share, fan engagement rate, sponsorship ROI, merchandise sell-through rate, athlete performance index. Captures KPI code, name, business unit owner, calculation methodology description, target threshold, unit of measure, reporting frequency, data source domain, and governance approval status. This is the authoritative reference for what each KPI means and how it is measured — not the computed values themselves.' .

ind:KpiTarget rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Kpi Target' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic KPI target and threshold records linking a KPI definition to a specific business unit, season, or fiscal period with its planned target value, stretch target, minimum acceptable threshold, and variance tolerance. Captures target setting date, approved-by stakeholder, target basis (prior year actuals, board mandate, market benchmark), and target revision history flag. Enables variance analysis between actuals and plan without storing computed actuals here.' .

ind:FanBehaviorModel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Behavior Model' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for each fan behavioral segmentation and predictive model deployed within the Sports Entertainment analytics platform — churn propensity model, upsell likelihood model, attendance prediction model, content affinity model. Captures model name, model type (classification, regression, clustering, recommendation), owning data science team, training dataset description, feature set summary, model version, deployment status (development, staging, production, retired), champion/challenger flag, and business use case. This is the model registry — not the scored output.' .

ind:ModelRun rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Model Run' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each execution of a fan behavior or predictive analytics model. Captures model reference, run timestamp, triggering pipeline or schedule, input dataset snapshot reference, number of records scored, run duration, infrastructure resource consumed (DBU), run status (success, failed, partial), output dataset location in the lakehouse, and data science engineer who initiated the run. Enables model performance monitoring, cost tracking, and lineage auditing for all ML pipeline executions.' .

ind:FanScore rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Fan Score' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Scored output record produced by fan behavior models for individual fan profiles — lifetime value score (LTV), attendance propensity score, merchandise affinity score, churn risk score, upsell readiness score, content engagement score. Captures fan profile reference, model reference, model run reference, score value, score percentile band, score date, score expiry date, and confidence interval. One record per fan per model per run. Consumed by CRM, personalization, and marketing activation workflows.' .

ind:AudienceMeasurement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Audience Measurement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Broadcast and digital audience measurement records capturing viewership, reach, and engagement metrics per event and broadcast window — Nielsen linear TV ratings, OTT concurrent streams, average minute audience (AMA), total unique viewers, peak concurrent viewers, completion rate, and share of voice. Captures measurement source (Nielsen, Comscore, internal OTT telemetry), measurement methodology, geographic market, demographic breakdown reference, broadcast channel reference, and event reference. SSOT for audience performance data consumed by broadcast rights valuation and sponsorship ROI.' .

ind:AudienceDemographic rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Audience Demographic' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Demographic profile breakdown records associated with audience measurement events — age band distribution, gender split, household income quintile, geographic DMA region, ethnicity index, and platform device type breakdown. Captures measurement source, audience measurement reference, demographic dimension type, dimension value, percentage share, and index vs. general population. Enables audience composition analysis for broadcast rights negotiations, sponsor targeting, and content strategy.' .

ind:PerformanceAnalyticsSnapshot rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Performance Analytics Snapshot' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Athlete and team performance analytics snapshot record aggregating advanced statistical metrics at the game or season level for analytical consumption — WAR (Wins Above Replacement), EPA (Expected Points Added), xG (Expected Goals), DVOA, PER, OPS+, and sport-specific advanced metrics. Captures athlete or team reference, fixture reference, season reference, sport discipline, metric name, metric value, metric percentile rank within league, and data source system. Serves as the Silver Layer analytical record for performance intelligence consumed by coaching staff dashboards and scouting platforms.' .

ind:PipelineDefinition rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Pipeline Definition' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master registry of all data science and analytics pipelines operating within the Sports Entertainment Databricks Lakehouse — fan scoring pipelines, audience measurement ingestion pipelines, performance analytics ETL, KPI computation pipelines, and recommendation engine pipelines. Captures pipeline name, owning team, source domain(s), target domain, schedule (cron expression), SLA window, pipeline type (batch, streaming, ML training, ML inference), technology stack (Databricks, dbt, Spark Structured Streaming), and current operational status.' .

ind:PipelineRun rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Pipeline Run' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each execution of a registered analytics or data science pipeline. Captures pipeline definition reference, run start timestamp, run end timestamp, trigger type (scheduled, manual, event-driven), run status (running, succeeded, failed, cancelled), records processed, records rejected, Databricks job run ID, cluster configuration reference, error message if failed, and data quality check pass/fail flag. Enables SLA monitoring, cost attribution, and operational reliability tracking for the analytics platform.' .

ind:InsightRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Insight Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Business intelligence and analytics insight request record capturing ad-hoc and recurring analytical requests submitted by business stakeholders across Sports Entertainment — executive dashboard requests, pre-event fan behavior briefs, sponsorship valuation analyses, broadcast rights negotiation data packages. Captures requestor name and business unit, request description, priority level, requested delivery date, assigned analyst, request status (submitted, in-progress, delivered, cancelled), and output format (dashboard, dataset, presentation, API feed).' .

ind:DashboardDefinition rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Dashboard Definition' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all executive and operational dashboards published across Sports Entertainment — CEO performance dashboard, venue operations dashboard, fan engagement scorecard, broadcast audience dashboard, sponsorship fulfillment tracker. Captures dashboard name, owning business unit, BI platform (Tableau, Power BI, Databricks SQL), refresh frequency, primary KPI references, target audience role, publication status (draft, published, archived), and data domain sources. This is the dashboard registry — not the rendered dashboard itself.' .

ind:FeatureStoreEntity rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Feature Store Entity' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master registry of ML feature store entities managed within the Sports Entertainment Databricks Feature Store — fan features (recency, frequency, monetary), athlete features (form index, injury risk), event features (rivalry score, weather impact), and venue features (capacity utilization trend). Captures feature name, feature group, owning model or pipeline, data type, computation logic description, update frequency, point-in-time correctness flag, and feature store table location. Enables feature reuse, governance, and lineage tracking across all ML models.' .

ind:Experiment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Experiment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Data science experiment record tracking hypothesis-driven analytical investigations and model development experiments within the Sports Entertainment MLflow tracking environment. Captures experiment name, hypothesis statement, owning data scientist, start date, end date, experiment status (active, completed, abandoned), primary evaluation metric, best run reference, conclusion summary, and promotion decision (promote to production, abandon, iterate). Distinct from platform.ab_test which covers fan-facing UX experiments — this covers internal data science model experiments.' .

ind:AttributionModel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Attribution Model' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for revenue and fan conversion attribution models defining how credit for fan acquisition, ticket purchase, merchandise sale, or subscription conversion is allocated across marketing touchpoints and channels — first-touch, last-touch, linear, time-decay, and data-driven attribution models. Captures model name, attribution type, lookback window, channel weighting configuration description, owning marketing analytics team, deployment status, and business use case (ticket sales attribution, sponsorship influence attribution, broadcast subscription attribution).' .

ind:AttributionResult rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Attribution Result' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional output record of a marketing attribution model run assigning conversion credit to specific fan touchpoints and channels. Captures fan profile reference, conversion event type (ticket purchase, subscription signup, merchandise order), conversion event reference, attribution model reference, attributed channel, attributed campaign reference, credit weight assigned (0.0–1.0), attributed revenue value, and attribution run date. Enables ROI measurement for marketing spend across digital, broadcast, and venue channels.' .

ind:ForecastModel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Forecast Model' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for business forecasting models deployed across Sports Entertainment — ticket sales forecast, broadcast viewership forecast, merchandise demand forecast, sponsorship revenue forecast, venue attendance forecast. Captures model name, forecast horizon (days/weeks/seasons), forecast granularity (event-level, weekly, monthly), model algorithm (ARIMA, Prophet, XGBoost, LSTM), owning business unit, training data period, last retrain date, and deployment status. Distinct from fan_behavior_model which covers fan-level propensity scoring.' .

ind:ForecastOutput rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Forecast Output' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of forecast values produced by a deployed forecasting model for a specific business metric, time period, and business unit. Captures forecast model reference, forecast run reference, forecast period start and end date, business metric (ticket revenue, attendance, viewership, merchandise units), business unit or event reference, point forecast value, lower confidence interval, upper confidence interval, and actuals value once available for variance tracking. Consumed by FP&A, venue operations, and commercial teams.' .

ind:EngagementIndex rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Analytics ;
    rdfs:label 'Engagement Index' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic fan engagement index record computing a composite engagement score for a fan segment, league, venue, or event — combining attendance frequency, digital platform activity, merchandise purchase recency, loyalty program participation, social media interaction, and broadcast consumption signals into a normalized index value. Captures index period (weekly, monthly, seasonal), entity type (fan segment, franchise, event), entity reference, composite index value, component score breakdown by dimension, and index trend direction vs. prior period. Serves as the Silver Layer engagement health record for executive dashboards.' .

ind:BettingMarket rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Betting Market' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all wagering market definitions available across sports and entertainment events — covering moneyline, spread, totals (over/under), futures, parlays, teasers, and live in-play markets. Captures market type code, sport/league scope, settlement rules, market status (open, suspended, closed, settled), minimum/maximum stake limits, and jurisdiction availability flags. SSOT for all market definitions consumed by odds feeds, prop bet catalogs, and regulatory reporting.' .

ind:OddsFeed rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Odds Feed' ;
    rdfs:comment 'High-frequency transactional record of odds price updates received from odds compilers and third-party odds providers (e.g., Sportradar, Kambi) for each betting market. Captures market ID, selection ID, decimal/fractional/American odds format values, implied probability, line movement direction, feed source, timestamp of update, and feed status. Supports real-time odds display, line movement analytics, and audit trails for regulatory compliance.' .

ind:Wager rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Wager' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core transactional record of every individual bet placed by a registered bettor across all wagering channels — retail sportsbook, mobile app, kiosk, and online platform. Captures bettor account ID, betting market ID, selection, stake amount, odds at time of placement, potential payout, wager type (straight, parlay, teaser, prop), placement channel, placement timestamp, wager status (pending, won, lost, void, cashed out), settlement amount, and settlement timestamp. Primary transactional entity for sportsbook operations and regulatory reporting.' .

ind:BettorAccount rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Bettor Account' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Gaming-domain operational account record for each registered bettor on the sportsbook or fantasy platform. Distinct from fan.fan_profile (the enterprise identity SSOT) — this entity captures gaming-specific account attributes: account number, KYC verification status, age verification status, identity document reference, account tier (standard, VIP, professional), deposit limit settings, self-exclusion status, responsible gaming flags, jurisdiction of registration, account open date, and account balance. Links to fan.fan_profile via FK in the linking step.' .

ind:PropBet rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Prop Bet' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of proposition bet offerings — player props (anytime touchdown scorer, first basket, strikeout totals), game props (first team to score, margin of victory), and novelty/entertainment props. Captures prop bet code, description, associated event/fixture, player or team subject, prop category, market open/close timestamps, settlement criteria, and jurisdiction availability. Distinct from betting_market (which covers standard market types) — prop_bet is the specific offering catalog for proposition wagering.' .

ind:ParlayLeg rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Parlay Leg' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Association entity capturing each individual selection (leg) within a multi-leg parlay or teaser wager. Carries its own business data: leg sequence number, betting market ID, selection, odds at time of placement, leg status (pending, won, lost, void, pushed), settlement result, and contribution to combined parlay odds. Required for parlay settlement processing, regulatory reporting of multi-leg wagers, and responsible gaming monitoring of complex bet structures.' .

ind:FantasyLeague rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Fantasy League' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for each fantasy sports league instance — public, private, and corporate leagues across NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, and other sports. Captures league name, sport, season, scoring format (standard, PPR, half-PPR, dynasty, DFS), draft type (snake, auction, auto-pick), roster configuration, entry fee, prize pool structure, commissioner account ID, league status (forming, active, completed), and platform (DraftKings, FanDuel, proprietary). SSOT for fantasy league definitions.' .

ind:FantasyRoster rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Fantasy Roster' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of a fantasy team\'s active roster at a point in time within a fantasy league season. Captures fantasy team ID, fantasy league ID, roster week/period, each rostered athlete slot (QB, RB, WR, FLEX, etc.), athlete ID, acquisition type (drafted, waiver, trade, free agent pickup), acquisition date, and roster lock timestamp. Supports weekly lineup management, waiver processing, and season-long roster history.' .

ind:FantasyTeam rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Fantasy Team' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for each fantasy team registered within a fantasy league. Captures team name, owner bettor account ID, league ID, draft position, total points scored (season-to-date), wins/losses/ties record, waiver priority, trade block status, and team logo/branding. Distinct from fantasy_league (the league definition) and fantasy_roster (the weekly lineup). SSOT for fantasy team identity and season-long standings.' .

ind:FantasyDraft rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Fantasy Draft' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of the fantasy league draft event and all individual pick selections. Captures draft event date/time, draft type, draft order, each pick\'s round number, overall pick number, fantasy team making the pick, athlete selected, pick timestamp, and whether the pick was auto-selected. Supports draft history, draft grade analytics, and audit of athlete allocation across fantasy teams.' .

ind:FantasyTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Fantasy Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of all roster moves within a fantasy league — waiver claims, free agent pickups, drops, and trades between fantasy teams. Captures transaction type, initiating fantasy team, receiving fantasy team (for trades), athletes involved, transaction timestamp, waiver priority used, FAAB (Free Agent Acquisition Budget) amount spent, transaction status (pending, approved, vetoed, processed), and commissioner override flag.' .

ind:Wallet rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Wallet' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Financial ledger record for each bettor account\'s gaming wallet — tracking real-money balance, bonus balance, withdrawable balance, pending wager holds, and lifetime deposit/withdrawal totals. Captures wallet ID, bettor account ID, currency, current real-money balance, bonus credit balance, pending hold amount, last transaction timestamp, and wallet status. Distinct from fan.payment_method (stored payment instruments) — this is the in-platform gaming funds ledger.' .

ind:WalletTransaction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Wallet Transaction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional ledger entry for every movement of funds within a bettor\'s gaming wallet — deposits, withdrawals, wager stakes, wager settlements, bonus credits, bonus forfeitures, and adjustments. Captures transaction type, amount, currency, pre-transaction balance, post-transaction balance, reference wager ID or deposit ID, payment method reference, timestamp, and transaction status. Supports AML transaction monitoring, responsible gaming spend tracking, and financial reconciliation.' .

ind:Jurisdiction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Jurisdiction' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference master for all gaming regulatory jurisdictions in which Sports Entertainment holds or is pursuing a sports wagering or fantasy sports operating license. Captures jurisdiction code, jurisdiction name (state/province/country), license type (sports wagering, DFS, iGaming), regulatory body name, license number, license status (active, pending, suspended, expired), license expiry date, tax rate on gross gaming revenue (GGR), and applicable responsible gaming mandates. SSOT for jurisdiction-level compliance configuration.' .

ind:ResponsibleGamingLimit rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Responsible Gaming Limit' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of responsible gaming controls and self-imposed limits configured by a bettor account — deposit limits (daily/weekly/monthly), loss limits, wager limits, session time limits, cooling-off periods, and self-exclusion elections. Captures limit type, limit amount or duration, effective date, expiry date, limit status, source (player-initiated vs. operator-imposed vs. regulator-mandated), and jurisdiction context. Critical for regulatory compliance with responsible gaming mandates across all licensed jurisdictions.' .

ind:SelfExclusion rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Self Exclusion' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of a bettor\'s self-exclusion election or operator-imposed exclusion from gaming activities. Captures bettor account ID, exclusion type (voluntary self-exclusion, operator exclusion, state-mandated exclusion via NCPG/state exclusion lists), exclusion scope (single platform, all platforms, statewide), exclusion start date, exclusion end date (or permanent flag), reinstatement request date, reinstatement approval status, and jurisdiction. Distinct from responsible_gaming_limit — self-exclusion is a full account suspension, not a limit adjustment.' .

ind:RegulatoryReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Regulatory Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all regulatory reports submitted to gaming authorities across licensed jurisdictions — gross gaming revenue (GGR) reports, suspicious activity reports (SAR), self-exclusion compliance reports, responsible gaming program reports, and AML/KYC compliance filings. Captures report type, jurisdiction, reporting period, submission date, submitted by, report status (draft, submitted, acknowledged, under review, accepted), and regulatory body reference number. Supports multi-jurisdiction regulatory compliance operations.' .

ind:BonusOffer rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Bonus Offer' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of promotional bonus offers available to bettors — welcome bonuses, deposit match bonuses, free bet credits, odds boosts, parlay insurance, loyalty rewards, and referral bonuses. Captures offer code, offer type, bonus amount or percentage, minimum deposit trigger, wagering requirement (playthrough multiplier), eligible markets, eligible bettor segments, offer validity window, jurisdiction restrictions, and offer status. SSOT for all gaming promotional offer definitions.' .

ind:BonusRedemption rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Bonus Redemption' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of a bettor claiming and consuming a bonus offer. Captures bettor account ID, bonus offer ID, redemption timestamp, bonus amount credited, wagering requirement remaining, qualifying wager IDs, bonus expiry date, bonus status (active, wagering_in_progress, completed, expired, forfeited), and final bonus outcome (converted to real money or forfeited). Supports bonus liability tracking, promotional ROI measurement, and responsible gaming bonus monitoring.' .

ind:MarketSuspension rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Market Suspension' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each betting market suspension event — capturing market ID, suspension reason (injury news, line integrity concern, late team news, regulatory hold, technical issue), suspension timestamp, reinstatement timestamp, suspended by (automated risk engine or manual trader), and any associated wager void actions triggered. Supports trading desk operations, integrity monitoring, and audit trails for suspended market decisions.' .

ind:IntegrityAlert rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Integrity Alert' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record of suspicious wagering activity alerts generated by the integrity monitoring system — unusual line movement, abnormal betting volumes, correlated accounts, and match-fixing indicators. Captures alert type, triggering market/event, alert severity (low/medium/high/critical), detection timestamp, alert source (automated rules engine, manual trader flag, governing body notification), investigation status, assigned investigator, resolution outcome, and referral to governing body flag. Supports sports integrity programs and regulatory suspicious activity reporting.' .

ind:KycVerification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Kyc Verification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'KYC (Know Your Customer) identity verification record for each bettor account — capturing verification type (identity, age, address, source of funds), verification method (document upload, biometric, third-party bureau check via Jumio/Onfido), document type submitted, verification status (pending, approved, rejected, escalated), verification timestamp, verifying agent or system, rejection reason, and re-verification due date. Mandatory for AML compliance and gaming license obligations across all jurisdictions.' .

ind:Contest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Contest' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for Daily Fantasy Sports (DFS) contests and tournament-style gaming competitions — capturing contest name, sport, slate (game set), contest type (GPP/tournament, 50/50, head-to-head, satellite), entry fee, maximum entries per player, total entries cap, prize pool amount, prize pool structure (top-heavy vs. flat), contest start time, lock time, status (open, locked, live, completed, cancelled), and platform. Distinct from fantasy_league (season-long) — contest covers single-slate DFS competitions.' .

ind:ContestEntry rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Contest Entry' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of a bettor\'s entry into a DFS contest — capturing contest ID, bettor account ID, entry timestamp, entry fee paid, lineup submitted (athlete selections by position), total projected points, actual points scored, final rank, prize won, and payout status. Supports contest settlement, prize distribution, and multi-entry tracking for DFS regulatory compliance.' .

ind:Payout rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Payout' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of all gaming prize and winnings payouts disbursed to bettor accounts — covering wager settlements, DFS contest prizes, fantasy league prize distributions, and bonus conversions. Captures payout type, bettor account ID, wager or contest entry reference, gross payout amount, tax withholding amount (W-2G threshold compliance), net payout amount, payout method (wallet credit, check, ACH, wire), payout timestamp, and payout status. Supports financial reconciliation, tax reporting (IRS W-2G), and regulatory GGR calculations.' .

ind:Session rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Session' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each bettor\'s active gaming session on the sportsbook or DFS platform — capturing session start timestamp, session end timestamp, session duration, channel (mobile app, web, retail kiosk), device type, jurisdiction at time of session, number of wagers placed, total amount wagered, net session result (win/loss), and session termination reason (user logout, timeout, self-exclusion trigger). Supports responsible gaming session time monitoring, AML behavioral analysis, and platform engagement reporting.' .

ind:Credential rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Credential' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all security credentials issued to personnel operating at Sports Entertainment venues and events — staff badges, media passes, VIP access cards, contractor IDs, law enforcement credentials, and athlete/team credentials. Captures credential type, holder identity reference, issuing authority, validity period, access tier, biometric linkage flag, barcode/RFID identifier, revocation status, and chain-of-custody audit fields. SSOT for credential identity across all access control operations.' .

ind:AccessZone rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Access Zone' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all defined physical access control zones within Sports Entertainment venues — field/pitch level, locker rooms, press box, broadcast compound, VIP hospitality, back-of-house, command center, parking compounds, and public concourse zones. Captures zone code, zone name, venue reference, zone tier (public/restricted/secured/sterile), maximum occupancy, surveillance coverage flag, and zone adjacency metadata used for crowd flow modeling.' .

ind:CredentialAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Credential Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record linking a specific credential to an authorized holder for a defined event or period. Captures credential ID, holder type (staff, media, contractor, law enforcement, athlete, sponsor), event or venue scope, assignment date, assigned-by officer, pickup confirmation, return confirmation, and any special access annotations. Enables per-event credentialing workflows and post-event reconciliation.' .

ind:AccessEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Access Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'High-volume transactional record of every physical access control scan event at venue entry and internal zone checkpoints — credential presented, zone accessed, timestamp, scan result (granted/denied/flagged), reader device ID, officer override flag, and denial reason code. Feeds real-time occupancy tracking, post-event forensic review, and compliance audit trails. Distinct from ticketing.gate_scan which covers fan ticket entitlement scanning.' .

ind:ScreeningCheckpoint rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Screening Checkpoint' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all physical security screening checkpoints deployed at Sports Entertainment venues — magnetometer lanes, bag check stations, pat-down areas, vehicle inspection points, and credentialing desks. Captures checkpoint code, venue zone assignment, checkpoint type, equipment deployed (WTMD, X-ray, ETD), staffing requirement, throughput capacity (persons/hour), activation schedule, and ADA-accessible lane flag.' .

ind:ScreeningEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Screening Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of individual fan or personnel screening interactions at security checkpoints — capturing checkpoint ID, timestamp, screening outcome (cleared/secondary screening/denied entry/prohibited item confiscated), prohibited item type if applicable, officer ID, and escalation flag. Supports post-event security review, prohibited item trend analysis, and checkpoint throughput reporting.' .

ind:Post rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Post' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all defined security officer posts and patrol assignments within Sports Entertainment venues — fixed posts (gate, tunnel, field perimeter, command center), roving patrol zones, and mobile response positions. Captures post code, venue zone, post type, required staffing level, shift window, post priority tier, and radio channel assignment. Used for event-day staffing deployment and post coverage gap analysis.' .

ind:PostAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Post Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record linking security personnel to specific security posts for a given event or shift. Captures post ID, assigned officer (workforce reference), event reference, shift start/end times, check-in confirmation, check-out confirmation, relief officer reference, and any post-specific briefing notes. Enables real-time post coverage visibility and post-event staffing reconciliation.' .

ind:SecurityIncident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Security Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Core transactional record for all security incidents occurring at Sports Entertainment venues and events — fan altercations, ejections, prohibited item seizures, field invasions, credentialing violations, threats, suspicious packages, and law enforcement interventions. Captures incident type, severity tier, location (zone/section/gate), involved parties, responding officers, law enforcement notification flag, medical referral flag, narrative, disposition, and case closure status. Distinct from venue.safety_incident which covers physical safety/OSHA events.' .

ind:EjectionRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Ejection Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of every fan or personnel ejection from a Sports Entertainment venue or event. Captures ejection date/time, venue zone, reason code (intoxication, fighting, field invasion, harassment, prohibited item), ejecting officer, law enforcement handoff flag, ban recommendation flag, originating security incident reference, and fan account reference for ban enforcement. Feeds the venue ban registry and repeat offender tracking.' .

ind:VenueBan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue Ban' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record of all active and historical venue bans and trespass orders issued against individuals by Sports Entertainment. Captures banned individual identity (fan account or external person reference), ban type (event-specific, season, permanent), issuing venue, ban start/end dates, reason, originating ejection or incident reference, law enforcement trespass order number, reinstatement eligibility flag, and ban status. SSOT for ban enforcement across all venue access control operations.' .

ind:CrowdManagementPlan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Crowd Management Plan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for crowd management and ingress/egress operational plans developed for each event or venue configuration. Captures plan version, event reference, venue configuration, crowd flow strategy, entry gate activation schedule, expected peak ingress time, maximum safe occupancy thresholds by zone, emergency evacuation routes, and approval sign-off by venue security director. Serves as the operational blueprint for event-day crowd control.' .

ind:OccupancySnapshot rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Occupancy Snapshot' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Periodic transactional record capturing real-time venue occupancy counts by access zone during an event. Captures event reference, zone ID, snapshot timestamp, current occupancy count, maximum capacity, occupancy percentage, data source (gate scan aggregation, manual count, sensor feed), and alert flag when approaching capacity thresholds. Enables live crowd density monitoring and supports emergency response decision-making.' .

ind:SurveillanceCamera rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Surveillance Camera' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all CCTV and surveillance camera assets deployed across Sports Entertainment venues. Captures camera ID, venue zone coverage, camera type (fixed, PTZ, body-worn, drone), resolution tier, recording system reference, retention period (days), operational status, last maintenance date, and integration with video analytics platform. SSOT for surveillance infrastructure inventory distinct from venue.bms_system which covers broader building systems.' .

ind:SurveillanceFootageRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Surveillance Footage Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of requests to retrieve, preserve, or share surveillance footage for security investigations, law enforcement requests, or legal proceedings. Captures requesting party (internal officer, law enforcement agency, legal counsel), event or date/time range, camera IDs requested, footage purpose, chain-of-custody log, legal hold flag, disclosure authorization, and fulfillment status. Supports evidence management and legal compliance.' .

ind:EmergencyResponsePlan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Emergency Response Plan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all emergency response plans governing Sports Entertainment venues and events — active shooter protocols, bomb threat procedures, mass casualty incident (MCI) response, fire evacuation, severe weather shelter-in-place, and medical emergency escalation. Captures plan type, venue scope, version, activation triggers, command structure, law enforcement coordination contacts, medical triage zone assignments, and regulatory approval status (DHS, local fire marshal).' .

ind:EmergencyActivation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Emergency Activation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each emergency response plan activation at a Sports Entertainment venue or event. Captures activation timestamp, plan activated, activating authority, event reference, incident trigger description, command post location, agencies notified (police, fire, EMS, FBI), evacuation initiated flag, all-clear timestamp, after-action report reference, and casualties/injuries count. SSOT for emergency response execution history.' .

ind:LawEnforcementDeployment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Law Enforcement Deployment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of law enforcement agency deployments coordinated for Sports Entertainment events — local police, state police, federal agencies (FBI, DHS, Secret Service), and private security contractors. Captures agency name, deployment type (perimeter, inside venue, mounted, K9, plainclothes), officer count, deployment start/end times, command liaison contact, mutual aid agreement reference, and post-event debrief notes.' .

ind:ThreatAssessment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Threat Assessment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for formal threat assessments conducted for Sports Entertainment events, venues, or individuals of concern. Captures assessment type (event-level, venue-level, person-of-interest), threat category (terrorism, targeted violence, cyber-physical), threat level rating, intelligence sources, recommended countermeasures, DHS/FBI coordination flag, assessment author, review date, and disposition. Feeds event security planning and law enforcement briefing packages.' .

ind:ProhibitedItem rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Prohibited Item' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference catalog of all prohibited items defined in Sports Entertainment venue security policies — weapons categories, prohibited containers, laser pointers, drones, professional camera equipment, and event-specific restrictions. Captures item category, item description, prohibition type (absolute/conditional), applicable venue types, regulatory basis (DHS, league policy, local ordinance), confiscation protocol, and effective date. Used to standardize screening checkpoint enforcement.' .

ind:ConfiscationRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Confiscation Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of every prohibited item confiscated at a Sports Entertainment venue screening checkpoint or during an in-venue security response. Captures item type (prohibited_item reference), confiscation location, confiscating officer, event reference, owner identity (if provided), storage disposition (destroyed, held for retrieval, turned over to law enforcement), and chain-of-custody log. Supports post-event prohibited item trend reporting and policy calibration.' .

ind:Briefing rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Briefing' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for pre-event security briefings conducted with security staff, law enforcement liaisons, and venue operations teams. Captures event reference, briefing date/time, briefing officer, attendee count by role category, threat level communicated, key operational directives issued, post assignments reviewed, emergency plan version referenced, and acknowledgment sign-off status. Ensures documented pre-event security coordination and briefing compliance.' .

ind:AfterActionReport rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'After Action Report' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Post-event security review and after-action report record capturing the formal security debrief for each Sports Entertainment event. Captures event reference, report author, total incidents by category, ejection count, law enforcement assists, screening throughput statistics, crowd management performance notes, equipment failures, recommended policy changes, and sign-off by venue security director. Feeds continuous improvement of security operations and regulatory compliance documentation.' .

ind:SecurityContract rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Security Contract' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for commercial agreements with private security service providers and guard companies engaged by Sports Entertainment for venue and event security operations. Captures vendor reference, contract type (event-specific, annual retainer, master services), service scope (staffing, K9, executive protection, crowd management), contracted headcount, billing rate structure, performance SLA terms, insurance and licensing requirements, and contract status. Distinct from partner.vendor_contract which covers general vendor supply agreements.' .

ind:StaffingPlan rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Staffing Plan' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for event-level security staffing plans defining the total security workforce deployment for a specific event. Captures event reference, venue reference, total security headcount by role (screening officers, post guards, supervisors, K9 handlers, law enforcement liaisons), private security vendor allocation, law enforcement requested count, staffing approval status, and budget reference. Serves as the authoritative staffing blueprint used to drive post_assignment and law_enforcement_deployment records.' .

ind:IpPortfolio rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Ip Portfolio' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for Sports Entertainment\'s intellectual property portfolio assets — trademarks, service marks, trade dress, patents, copyrights, and domain names. Captures IP asset type, registration number, jurisdiction, filing date, registration date, expiration date, renewal deadline, owner entity (league, franchise, venue), IP class (Nice Classification for trademarks), status (pending, registered, abandoned, expired), licensing eligibility flag, estimated valuation, and managing outside counsel reference. SSOT for all IP assets owned or co-owned by Sports Entertainment entities.' .

ind:TrademarkRegistration rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Trademark Registration' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Granular trademark registration record for each mark filed or registered by Sports Entertainment across global jurisdictions. Captures mark name, mark type (word, figurative, combined, 3D), Nice class codes, filing jurisdiction (USPTO, EUIPO, WIPO Madrid Protocol), application number, registration number, filing date, publication date, registration date, renewal date, opposition period end date, current prosecution status, associated IP portfolio reference, and assigned trademark counsel. Tracks the full prosecution lifecycle from application through registration and maintenance.' .

ind:IpEnforcementAction rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Ip Enforcement Action' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of every IP enforcement action initiated or defended by Sports Entertainment — cease and desist letters, UDRP domain disputes, trademark opposition proceedings, copyright takedown notices (DMCA), and infringement litigation. Captures action type, target party, infringing asset description, jurisdiction, filing date, enforcement channel (USPTO TTAB, federal court, WIPO, platform takedown), current status, outcome, damages sought, settlement terms, and assigned outside counsel. Links to the relevant IP portfolio asset and any associated litigation case.' .

ind:LitigationCase rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Litigation Case' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all active and historical litigation matters involving Sports Entertainment as plaintiff or defendant — commercial disputes, employment claims, personal injury suits, antitrust actions, labor arbitrations, and regulatory enforcement proceedings. Captures case name, case number, court or tribunal, jurisdiction, case type, filing date, service date, discovery cutoff, trial date, current status (pre-litigation, discovery, trial, appeal, settled, closed), opposing party, opposing counsel, assigned in-house counsel, outside counsel firm, estimated exposure, reserve amount, and final disposition. SSOT for all litigation matters distinct from compliance arbitration cases.' .

ind:LitigationEvent rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Litigation Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of every significant procedural event within a litigation case — complaint filing, answer, motion to dismiss, summary judgment motion, deposition, mediation session, hearing, trial day, verdict, appeal filing, and settlement execution. Captures case reference, event type, event date, description, filing party, court docket number, outcome or ruling, next deadline triggered, and responsible attorney. Enables full docket tracking and deadline management within each litigation matter.' .

ind:Hold rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Hold' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for litigation hold notices issued to preserve electronically stored information (ESI) and physical documents relevant to active or anticipated litigation. Captures hold name, triggering matter (litigation case or regulatory investigation), issue date, custodian count, data sources placed on hold (email, SharePoint, Slack, Veeva), hold status (active, released, suspended), release date, and issuing counsel. Critical for eDiscovery compliance and spoliation defense. Links to litigation cases and affected workforce members as custodians.' .

ind:ContractTemplate rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Contract Template' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master library of standardized contract templates managed by the legal department for use across Sports Entertainment business units — athlete NIL agreement templates, venue rental agreements, broadcast rights term sheets, sponsorship deal frameworks, merchandise licensing templates, employment offer letter templates, NDA templates, and vendor MSA templates. Captures template name, contract category, version number, effective date, approved-for-use flag, jurisdiction applicability, required approval workflow, template owner (in-house counsel), and last review date. Distinct from executed contract instances which reside in their respective operational domains.' .

ind:Matter rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Matter' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Unified master record for all legal matters managed by the in-house legal department that do not rise to the level of formal litigation — regulatory inquiries, pre-litigation disputes, transactional advisory matters, M&A due diligence projects, internal investigations, and general counsel advisory engagements. Captures matter name, matter type, business unit requesting legal support, assigned in-house counsel, outside counsel engagement reference, open date, target close date, current status, matter description, estimated legal spend, and actual legal spend to date. Serves as the top-level matter management record linking to all subordinate legal activities.' .

ind:OutsideCounsel rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Outside Counsel' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all outside law firms and individual attorneys engaged by Sports Entertainment for legal services. Captures firm name, firm type (AmLaw 100, boutique, regional), primary practice areas (IP, labor, litigation, M&A, gaming regulation), billing rate card, preferred vendor status, conflict check status, engagement jurisdictions, primary relationship partner, billing contact, diversity certification, and panel counsel designation. SSOT for outside counsel identity distinct from the broader vendor master in the partner domain — legal-specific attributes justify a dedicated record.' .

ind:CounselEngagement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Counsel Engagement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each formal outside counsel engagement issued by Sports Entertainment for a specific legal matter. Captures engagement letter date, scope of work, billing arrangement (hourly, flat fee, contingency, blended rate), matter reference, outside counsel firm reference, lead attorney, billing rate approved, budget cap, actual spend to date, invoice count, engagement status (active, closed, suspended), and approving in-house counsel. Enables legal spend management and outside counsel performance tracking per matter.' .

ind:Invoice rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Invoice' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Outside counsel invoice record submitted for legal services rendered on a specific matter engagement. Captures invoice number, billing period, outside counsel firm, matter reference, engagement reference, invoice date, total amount billed, amount approved, amount disputed, amount paid, billing timekeeper entries count, expense line count, UTBMS task code breakdown, invoice status (received, under review, approved, disputed, paid), and review notes from in-house counsel. Supports eBilling compliance (LEDES format) and legal spend analytics.' .

ind:InsurancePolicy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Insurance Policy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all corporate insurance policies held by Sports Entertainment — general liability, directors and officers (D&O), errors and omissions (E&O), cyber liability, event cancellation, athlete disability, workers compensation, property and casualty, and umbrella policies. Captures policy number, insurer name, policy type, coverage category, policy period start and end dates, premium amount, deductible, coverage limit, named insureds, endorsements, broker name, renewal date, and claims-made vs occurrence designation. SSOT for all insurance coverage managed by the legal and risk management function.' .

ind:InsuranceClaim rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Insurance Claim' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of every insurance claim filed by or against Sports Entertainment under a corporate insurance policy. Captures claim number, policy reference, claim type, incident date, claim filing date, claimant identity, claim description, claimed amount, reserve amount, insurer claim handler, assigned in-house counsel, litigation case reference (if claim escalates), current claim status (open, under investigation, settled, closed, denied), settlement amount, and payment date. Enables risk management tracking and insurance recovery monitoring.' .

ind:CorporateEntity rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Corporate Entity' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for every legal entity within the Sports Entertainment corporate structure — parent holding companies, league operating entities, franchise LLCs, venue operating companies, broadcast subsidiaries, and joint ventures. Captures entity name, entity type (LLC, LP, Corp, JV), jurisdiction of incorporation, EIN/tax ID, registered agent, registered address, formation date, dissolution date (if applicable), ownership percentage, parent entity reference, active status, and governing law. SSOT for corporate entity identity supporting governance, intercompany transactions, and regulatory filings.' .

ind:BoardResolution rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Board Resolution' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all formal board of directors and member resolutions passed by Sports Entertainment corporate entities. Captures resolution number, entity reference, resolution type (approval, authorization, ratification, amendment), resolution date, meeting type (regular, special, written consent), quorum achieved flag, vote outcome (unanimous, majority, dissenting votes count), resolution subject matter, authorized signatories, effective date, and document storage reference. Supports corporate governance documentation and authorized signatory management.' .

ind:GovernanceDocument rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Governance Document' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master catalog of all corporate governance documents maintained by the legal department — articles of incorporation, operating agreements, bylaws, shareholder agreements, franchise agreements (league-level), joint venture agreements, and partnership agreements. Captures document name, document type, governing entity reference, execution date, effective date, expiration date (if applicable), version number, amendment count, governing law jurisdiction, counterparty names, document status (draft, executed, superseded, terminated), and secure document repository reference. Distinct from contract templates (which are reusable forms) and executed operational contracts (which reside in their respective domains).' .

ind:Nda rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Nda' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all Non-Disclosure Agreements executed by Sports Entertainment — mutual NDAs with prospective partners, one-way NDAs with vendors, athlete and employee confidentiality agreements, and M&A transaction NDAs. Captures NDA type (mutual, one-way), counterparty name, counterparty type (vendor, athlete, employee, investor, media partner), execution date, effective date, expiration date, auto-renewal flag, confidentiality scope description, permitted disclosure exceptions, governing law, dispute resolution mechanism, and assigned in-house counsel. Enables proactive expiration management and confidentiality obligation tracking.' .

ind:RegulatoryLicense rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Regulatory License' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all operational licenses and regulatory permits required to conduct Sports Entertainment business activities — gaming operator licenses, broadcast licenses (FCC), liquor licenses (venue-level), event permits, venue operating certificates, and sports wagering licenses by jurisdiction. Captures license type, issuing regulatory authority, license number, licensed entity reference, jurisdiction, issue date, expiration date, renewal application deadline, renewal status, license fee, conditions or restrictions, compliance officer responsible, and suspension/revocation history. Distinct from compliance.license_permit which tracks broader compliance obligations — this record is owned by legal as the licensing authority relationship manager.' .

ind:Deadline rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Deadline' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record tracking all critical legal deadlines across matters, litigation cases, IP registrations, contract renewals, and regulatory filings managed by the legal department. Captures deadline type (statute of limitations, response due, renewal filing, discovery cutoff, contract expiration, license renewal), associated matter or asset reference, deadline date, reminder trigger dates, responsible attorney, completion status, completion date, and escalation flag. Enables proactive deadline management and prevents missed filings or expirations across the legal portfolio.' .

ind:PowerOfAttorney rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Power Of Attorney' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all powers of attorney and authorized signatory instruments executed by Sports Entertainment corporate entities — general POAs, limited POAs for specific transactions, IP prosecution POAs filed with patent and trademark offices, and banking authorization instruments. Captures POA type, grantor entity, grantee name and role, scope of authority, execution date, effective date, expiration date, revocation date, notarization status, jurisdiction, and document repository reference. Supports authorized signatory management and IP prosecution authority tracking.' .

ind:SpendBudget rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Spend Budget' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Annual and matter-level legal spend budget record tracking approved legal department expenditure allocations across outside counsel, litigation reserves, IP prosecution fees, insurance premiums, and regulatory filing fees. Captures budget period, budget category (outside counsel, IP fees, litigation reserve, insurance, regulatory), business unit or matter reference, approved budget amount, committed spend, actual spend to date, variance, budget owner (General Counsel or Deputy GC), approval date, and last reforecast date. Enables legal department financial management and outside counsel spend governance.' .

ind:ContractObligation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Contract Obligation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Operational record tracking specific contractual obligations and commitments extracted from executed contracts across all business domains — payment milestones, performance deliverables, reporting requirements, notice obligations, renewal options, and termination rights. Captures obligation type, source contract reference (with domain pointer), obligor party, obligee party, obligation description, due date, recurrence pattern (one-time, annual, quarterly), completion status, completion date, and responsible business owner. Enables cross-domain contract obligation management and proactive compliance with contractual commitments.' .

ind:Opinion rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Opinion' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for formal legal opinions and memoranda issued by in-house counsel or outside counsel to Sports Entertainment business units — gaming regulatory opinions, tax opinions, employment law guidance, IP clearance opinions, antitrust risk assessments, and M&A due diligence legal memos. Captures opinion title, opinion type, requesting business unit, issuing counsel (in-house or outside firm), issue date, subject matter, jurisdiction, conclusion summary, reliance limitations, confidentiality classification, and document repository reference. Enables legal knowledge management and precedent tracking.' .

ind:SettlementAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Legal ;
    rdfs:label 'Settlement Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for all settlement agreements resolving litigation cases, IP disputes, employment claims, and regulatory enforcement actions. Captures settlement date, settling parties, matter or case reference, settlement type (monetary, injunctive, consent decree, confidential), settlement amount, payment schedule, non-monetary terms (injunction scope, behavioral commitments), confidentiality clause flag, non-disparagement clause flag, governing law, execution date, and compliance monitoring requirements. Distinct from litigation_case (which tracks the full matter lifecycle) — this record captures the binding resolution instrument.' .

ind:EsportsTeam rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Esports Team' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for professional esports teams competing in Sports Entertainment-operated or affiliated esports leagues — capturing team name, game title, roster size, org affiliation, and competitive region.' .

ind:EsportsMatch rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Esports Match' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of each competitive esports match played within Sports Entertainment esports leagues — capturing game title, teams, map/stage, result, VOD link, and tournament context.' .

ind:ContingentWorker rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Contingent Worker' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for non-employee contingent workforce members engaged by Sports Entertainment — freelance broadcast crew, event-day contractors, gig workers, and temporary staff not managed through standard employment contracts.' .

ind:CreatorProfile rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Creator Profile' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for content creators, influencers, and digital talent managed or partnered with Sports Entertainment — capturing creator identity, platform handles, audience metrics, content niche, and partnership status for influencer marketing and creator economy initiatives.' .

ind:InternationalFederation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'International Federation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master record for international sports governing bodies and their hierarchical structure — FIFA, IOC, World Athletics, ICC — capturing federation name, jurisdiction level (global/continental/national), parent federation reference, member associations, and governance authority scope.' .

ind:Venue rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Master reference table for venue. ' .

ind:CreatorDeal rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Creator Deal' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a sponsor and a creator_profile in the Sports Entertainment ecosystem. It captures the commercial terms, exclusivity scope, NIL agreement linkage, content rights territory, revenue share, and contract lifecycle for each unique sponsor-creator partnership. Each record links one sponsor to one creator_profile and holds attributes that exist only in the context of that specific commercial agreement — not on the sponsor master record nor on the creator profile master record.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, sponsors actively partner with multiple content creators (influencers, NIL athletes) for branded content campaigns simultaneously, and a creator works with multiple sponsors across different brands and categories at the same time. This relationship is operationally managed as a \'Sponsorship Deal\' or \'Creator Partnership\' — a recognized business contract with its own terms, exclusivity scope, NIL agreement references, revenue share percentages, flat fees, and contract dates that belong to neither the sponsor nor the creator alone. Business teams actively create, negotiate, amend, and terminate these agreements as distinct commercial records.' .

ind:Partnership rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Partnership' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the official contracted Partnership between a league and a vendor. It captures the operational record of each league-vendor partnership agreement including designation category, exclusivity scope, financial terms, and partnership lifecycle dates. Each record links one league to one vendor and carries attributes that exist only in the context of this specific partnership relationship — not on the league or vendor master records alone.. Existence Justification: In professional sports entertainment, leagues actively manage official partnerships with vendors — the NFL has an official ball supplier (Wilson), an official timing partner (Daktronics), and an official apparel partner (Nike), while Nike simultaneously holds official partnerships with the NFL, NBA, and MLB. This is a genuine operational M:N relationship where the business creates, manages, and terminates partnership agreements that carry their own financial terms, exclusivity scopes, and official designation categories. The relationship is not derivable from transactional data — it is a first-class business contract that procurement and league operations teams actively govern.' .

ind:IpLicenseGrant rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Ip License Grant' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the contractual IP License Grant between a vendor_contract and an ip_portfolio asset. It captures the specific authorization within a vendor agreement that grants a vendor rights to use a defined intellectual property asset under defined terms — including grant type, scope, territory, exclusivity, royalty rate, and license term dates. Each record links one vendor_contract to one ip_portfolio asset and carries attributes that exist only in the context of that specific vendor-IP pairing. Serves as the SSOT for all IP licensing provisions embedded within vendor commercial agreements.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, vendor contracts (e.g., broadcast technology, merchandise, digital platform agreements) routinely include IP licensing provisions that grant vendors rights to use specific trademarks, logos, broadcast rights, or other IP assets. A single vendor contract can license multiple IP assets simultaneously (e.g., a broadcast technology vendor licensed to use the league logo, team marks, and broadcast rights), and a single IP asset (e.g., the league trademark) can be licensed across many vendor contracts. The business actively manages these IP license grants as distinct operational records with their own terms, territory, exclusivity, and royalty rates.' .

ind:License rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'License' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a digital content asset and an external vendor (broadcaster, OTT platform, RSN, or distributor). It captures the formal licensing agreement under which Sports Entertainment grants a vendor the right to use a specific asset within defined territorial, exclusivity, and temporal boundaries. Each record links one asset to one vendor and carries the financial, geographic, and rights-scope attributes that exist only in the context of that specific license grant — not on the asset master or the vendor master alone.. Existence Justification: In sports-entertainment rights management, a single digital content asset (e.g., an NFL highlight reel) is simultaneously licensed to multiple vendors — a broadcast partner, an OTT platform, and a regional sports network — each under distinct territorial, exclusivity, and financial terms. Conversely, a single vendor (e.g., ESPN) holds active licenses to thousands of assets across multiple sports disciplines. The business actively creates, negotiates, renews, and terminates these license agreements as a core rights-management process, and each agreement carries its own fee, territory scope, exclusivity flag, and validity window that cannot reside on either the asset or vendor record alone.' .

ind:BudgetAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Budget Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Budget Allocation contract between a budget planning record and an organizational unit. It captures the formal assignment of planned, revised, committed, and forecast financial amounts — as well as approved headcount — to a specific org unit for a given fiscal period, budget version, and scenario. Each record links one budget to one org_unit and carries attributes that exist only in the context of this allocation relationship, including allocated amounts, headcount approvals, and allocation-level approval status. Managed jointly by Finance (FP&A) and HR as part of the annual budgeting, reforecast, and headcount planning cycles.. Existence Justification: In Sports Entertainment, a single budget record (e.g., FY2025 OPEX for Event Operations) is allocated across multiple org units (team ops, broadcast, venue, events), and each org unit receives funding from multiple budget line items across OPEX, CAPEX, and headcount categories. Finance and HR jointly manage these allocations as a formal business process — creating, revising, and approving budget allocations per org-unit-budget combination with tracked amounts, headcount approvals, and fiscal versioning. This is an operationally managed relationship, not an analytical derivation.' .

ind:RightsAgreement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Agreement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a broadcast channel and a league governing the rights to distribute league content. It captures the operational terms of each channel-league broadcast rights deal — including rights tier, exclusivity, territory, and effective dates — that exist only in the context of this specific channel-league pairing. Each record is a discrete, actively managed rights agreement that the business creates, renegotiates, and terminates as part of its media rights operations.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a single broadcast channel (e.g., ESPN) simultaneously carries multiple leagues (NFL, NBA, MLB), and a single league (e.g., NFL) is distributed across multiple channels (ESPN, Fox, NBC, CBS) under distinct rights agreements. The business actively manages these channel-league broadcast rights relationships as named contracts with their own attributes — rights tier, exclusivity type, territory, and effective dates — that belong to neither the channel nor the league alone. This is a genuine operational M:N where rights deals are created, renegotiated, and terminated as discrete business events.' .

ind:PositionCostAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Position Cost Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the funding contract between a position and a cost center in Sports Entertainment\'s workforce and financial planning model. It captures the split-funding arrangement by which a position\'s labor costs are distributed across one or more cost centers at defined allocation percentages and effective date ranges. Each record links one position to one cost center with attributes — allocation percentage, effective dates, budget approval status, headcount plan year, and pay grade — that exist only in the context of this specific position-to-cost-center funding relationship. Sourced from SAP CO labor distribution and SuccessFactors Position Management.. Existence Justification: In Sports Entertainment organizations, positions are routinely split-funded across multiple cost centers — e.g., a Head of Broadcast Operations charged 60% to the Broadcast Production cost center and 40% to the Venue Operations cost center. Conversely, each cost center funds multiple positions simultaneously. This split-funding arrangement is an actively managed operational record with its own attributes (allocation percentage, effective dates, budget approval status) that belong to neither the position nor the cost center alone.' .

ind:ChannelActivation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Channel Activation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a sponsorship deal and a distribution platform channel. It captures the specific commercial activation terms — impression commitments, CPM rates, exclusivity scope, and territory — that apply to a single deal on a single platform channel. Each record is an operationally managed entity created when a deal is activated on a channel, updated as delivery metrics are tracked, and closed when the activation period ends.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment sponsorship, a single deal (e.g., a digital platform partnership or broadcast integration) is contractually activated across multiple distribution platform channels simultaneously — an OTT app, a social media channel, and a broadcast slot may all be covered under one deal with distinct impression commitments and CPM rates per channel. Conversely, a single platform channel (e.g., ESPN+ OTT) carries activations from many concurrent sponsorship deals across different sponsors and deal types. The business actively manages these per-channel activation records, tracking impression commitments, CPM rates, exclusivity scope, and territory at the deal-channel intersection — data that belongs to neither the deal nor the channel alone.' .

ind:ContentPlacement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Content Placement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the in-venue content placement event between a facility and a digital content asset. It captures the operational and rights management record governing which asset is displayed in which physical zone of which venue, for what display window, under what rights clearance status, and approved by whom. Each record links one facility to one asset and carries attributes that exist only in the context of a specific placement — they cannot reside on the facility master or the asset master alone. Serves as the SSOT for in-venue digital signage scheduling, sponsor display rights compliance, and AV channel assignment across all Sports Entertainment venues.. Existence Justification: A facility (stadium, arena, amphitheater) actively displays digital content assets across multiple physical zones — scoreboards, concourse screens, suite AV systems, LED ribbon boards — and a single content asset (video highlight, promotional clip, sponsor creative) can be licensed and scheduled for display at many facilities simultaneously. The business operationally manages each facility-asset placement as a distinct record with its own display window, zone assignment, rights clearance status, and approval workflow. This is not an analytical correlation but an active content operations and rights management process.' .

ind:FacilityVendorEngagement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Facility Vendor Engagement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a physical venue facility and an external vendor providing services at that facility. It captures the operational service agreement governing which vendor delivers which service category at a given facility, including contractual terms, SLA commitments, and financial arrangements. Each record links one facility to one vendor for a specific service engagement, with attributes that exist only in the context of this facility-vendor service relationship. Serves as the SSOT for venue operator procurement teams managing the active vendor roster per facility.. Existence Justification: In sports-entertainment venue operations, a single facility (e.g., a stadium) is actively served by many vendors simultaneously — security firms, F&B operators, AV contractors, cleaning services, parking operators — each under distinct contractual terms. Conversely, a vendor (e.g., a regional security company) may hold active service agreements across multiple facilities in the same league portfolio. The business actively manages this relationship as a named operational concept — a vendor engagement or service contract — with its own lifecycle attributes (contract dates, SLA tier, revenue share, service category) that belong to neither the facility nor the vendor alone.' .

ind:VendorActivation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Activation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the operational Activation event between a fixture and a vendor. It captures the per-fixture engagement of an external vendor to deliver a specific service at a live event — including the service category, activation role, governing contract reference, accreditation clearance status, and on-site timing window. Each record links one fixture to one vendor for one service deployment, with attributes that exist only in the context of this fixture-vendor engagement and cannot reside on either the fixture or vendor master alone.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment operations, a single fixture (match, concert, PPV event) requires MANY vendors simultaneously — catering, security, AV/broadcast, merchandise, medical, transportation — each activated for that specific event. Conversely, a single vendor (e.g., a security firm or catering company) operates across MANY fixtures per season. The business actively manages per-fixture vendor activations as operational records with their own lifecycle: activation role, service category, accreditation status, and timing windows that belong to neither the fixture nor the vendor master alone.' .

ind:RevenueAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Revenue Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between franchise and revenue_stream. It captures the per-franchise, per-stream financial allocation record governing how each revenue stream is distributed to or generated by each franchise for a given season. Each record links one franchise to one revenue_stream with attributes — allocation percentage, revenue sharing rate, effective dates, and season year — that exist only in the context of this franchise-stream allocation agreement and cannot reside on either master entity alone.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a franchise actively participates in multiple revenue streams simultaneously (local broadcast rights, gate receipts, sponsorship, merchandise, gaming) while each revenue stream (particularly national broadcast deals, league-wide sponsorships) is distributed across multiple franchises. The business explicitly tracks per-franchise-stream allocation percentages, revenue sharing rates, and effective date ranges — this is an operationally managed financial allocation record, not a derived analytical correlation. Finance and league operations teams actively create, update, and close these allocation records each season.' .

ind:PlatformRightsGrant rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Platform Rights Grant' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between media_rights_deal and digital_touchpoint. It captures the formal authorization granting a specific digital touchpoint the right to deliver content under a specific media rights deal, including the platform-level rights type, exclusivity terms, effective period, territory scope, and revenue share applicable to that specific deal-touchpoint combination. Each record links one media_rights_deal to one digital_touchpoint with attributes that exist only in the context of this per-platform rights authorization.. Existence Justification: A media rights deal licenses content delivery rights to multiple digital touchpoints simultaneously (e.g., an NFL deal may cover the OTT app, web portal, and IPTV endpoint under different terms), and each digital touchpoint can be covered by multiple rights deals across different sports, leagues, and territories. The business actively manages which touchpoints are authorized to deliver which rights, with per-touchpoint exclusivity flags, territory scopes, and revenue share terms that belong neither to the deal nor the touchpoint alone. This is a recognized operational concept in broadcast rights licensing — the authorization or \'platform rights grant\' — that rights operations teams create, update, and enforce.' .

ind:CrewMemberAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Crew Member Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Role-based assignment between an individual official and an officiating crew for a specific game. It captures the full crew roster composition that the league officiating bureau actively manages — including each official\'s designated role, conflict-of-interest clearance status, individual performance evaluation, and substitution events. Each record links one official to one officiating crew with attributes that exist only in the context of this per-game, per-role assignment. Supports officiating quality management, CBA compliance, conflict-of-interest screening, and workload tracking at the individual official level.. Existence Justification: In professional sports, officiating crew composition is a genuine operational M:N relationship: each officiating crew is assembled from a pool of certified officials (a crew may have 5–8 officials), and each official works across many different crew assignments throughout a season. The league actively manages crew_member_assignment as a business concept — assigning specific roles (crew chief, referee, linesman, VAR operator), tracking conflict-of-interest clearance per assignment, and evaluating individual performance per game. The current officiating_crew product only captures crew_chief_official_id and var_operator_official_id as named FKs, which cannot represent the full crew roster and leaves all other officials untracked.' .

ind:PersonalizationRule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Fan ;
    rdfs:label 'Personalization Rule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Content Personalization Rule — the operational contract between a fan segment and a content asset within the sports entertainment personalization engine. Each record captures a deliberate, managed assignment of a specific digital content asset to a specific fan segment, including the activation window, priority ranking, A/B test variant, and rule logic governing delivery. Records are created, updated, and retired by CRM and content operations teams as part of campaign and DTC personalization workflows.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment personalization, content teams actively assign specific digital assets (video highlights, editorial articles, social media content) to fan segments as part of campaign and personalization workflows. A single fan segment (e.g., \'High-Value Season Ticket Holders\') can be targeted with many different content assets, and a single asset (e.g., a playoff highlight reel) can be assigned to multiple segments simultaneously. This relationship is operationally managed — marketers create, update, and retire these assignments with specific activation windows, priority rankings, and A/B test variants.' .

ind:AudienceTargetingAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Sponsorship ;
    rdfs:label 'Audience Targeting Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a sponsor and a fan_segment within the sponsorship audience planning process. It captures the operational record of a sponsor\'s contracted rights to reach a specific fan audience segment through defined activation channels, including targeting priority, category exclusivity, reach commitments, and contractual validity dates. Each record links one sponsor to one fan_segment with attributes that exist only in the context of this sponsor-segment targeting agreement.. Existence Justification: In sports-entertainment sponsorship operations, a sponsor actively targets multiple fan segments (e.g., a beer brand targets millennials, high-LTV fans, and season ticket holders simultaneously), and each fan segment is targeted by multiple sponsors across different industry categories. The business manages these pairings as named \'Audience Targeting\' or \'Sponsorship Audience Allocation\' records with contractual attributes — targeting priority, exclusivity rights per segment, activation channel, and contracted reach commitments — that belong to neither the sponsor nor the segment alone. This is an operationally managed relationship that sponsorship sales teams create, negotiate, and update as part of the audience planning and activation workflow.' .

ind:FootageCameraScope rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Security ;
    rdfs:label 'Footage Camera Scope' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the scoping event between a surveillance_footage_request and a surveillance_camera. It captures which specific cameras are included in a footage request and the per-camera retrieval details — time window, format, file size, and redaction status — that exist only in the context of a specific request-camera pairing. Each record links one surveillance_footage_request to one surveillance_camera and tracks the operational fulfillment state for that camera\'s footage within the request.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment security operations, a single footage request routinely spans multiple cameras (e.g., an incident investigation covering entrance cameras, concourse cameras, and VIP area cameras simultaneously). Conversely, a single camera will be referenced by many different footage requests over time — law enforcement requests, internal investigations, insurance claims. The business actively manages which specific cameras are included in each request, with per-camera attributes such as the footage time window, file size, format, and redaction status that belong to neither the request nor the camera alone.' .

ind:RevenueAttribution rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Revenue Attribution' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between asset and revenue_stream. It captures the operational record of how a specific digital content asset is monetised under a specific revenue stream, including the geographic territory, distribution platform, monetisation window, and allocated revenue amount. Each record links one asset to one revenue_stream with attributes that exist only in the context of this rights-window attribution relationship, supporting rights valuation, royalty calculation, and segment P&L reporting.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a single digital content asset (e.g., a broadcast highlight reel) genuinely generates revenue across multiple simultaneous streams — broadcast rights, OTT subscription, and PPV — while each revenue stream (e.g., \'Broadcast Rights\') contains revenue attributable to many distinct assets. Finance actively manages this relationship for rights valuation, royalty calculation, and P&L attribution, making it an operationally managed entity, not a derived analytical correlation. The relationship carries its own data (territory, platform, window dates, allocated revenue amounts) that belongs to neither the asset nor the revenue stream alone.' .

ind:MarketJurisdictionAvailability rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Gaming ;
    rdfs:label 'Market Jurisdiction Availability' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Authorization contract between betting_market and gaming_jurisdiction. It captures the explicit regulatory authorization (or exclusion) of a specific wagering market within a specific gaming jurisdiction, including availability lifecycle status, effective date range, jurisdiction-specific stake overrides, and exclusion reasons. Each record links one betting_market to one gaming_jurisdiction and carries attributes that exist only in the context of that specific market-jurisdiction pairing. This entity replaces the denormalized jurisdiction_availability and jurisdiction_exclusion STRING fields on betting_market and serves as the SSOT for compliance teams managing market geo-restriction matrices.. Existence Justification: In licensed sportsbook operations, each betting market must be explicitly authorized for each jurisdiction where it is offered — a single market (e.g., NFL moneyline) is available in multiple jurisdictions (NJ, PA, CO), and each jurisdiction hosts hundreds of active markets. Compliance teams actively manage this matrix, controlling availability status, effective dates, jurisdiction-specific stake limits, and exclusion reasons. The relationship is a recognized operational concept called \'Market Jurisdiction Availability\' or \'Market Geo-Restriction\' that is created, updated, and audited as part of regulatory compliance workflows.' .

ind:RightsWindowChannelAuthorization rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Broadcast ;
    rdfs:label 'Rights Window Channel Authorization' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between broadcast_rights_window and platform_channel. It captures the formal authorization record that grants a specific platform channel the right to distribute content under a specific broadcast rights window, including the technical compliance terms, exclusivity scope, DRM requirements, and stream limits that govern that specific channel-window combination. Each record links one broadcast_rights_window to one platform_channel with attributes that exist only in the context of this authorization relationship.. Existence Justification: In sports media rights operations, a single broadcast rights window (e.g., \'NFL Sunday Ticket, OTT, USA, 2024-2025\') is actively distributed across multiple platform channels simultaneously — an OTT app, an IPTV portal, and a DTC streaming endpoint may all be authorized under the same window. Conversely, a platform channel like ESPN+ carries content from dozens of distinct rights windows covering different leagues, territories, and time periods. Rights operations teams actively manage which channels are authorized under which windows, with per-combination terms such as exclusivity scope, DRM policy, and concurrent stream limits that belong to neither entity alone.' .

ind:JurisdictionLicense rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Workforce ;
    rdfs:label 'Jurisdiction License' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the regulatory licensing contract between an employee and a gaming jurisdiction. It captures the specific license or authorization held by an individual workforce member within a given gaming regulatory jurisdiction, including their assigned compliance role, the jurisdiction-issued license number, the effective and expiry dates of the authorization, and the current license status. Each record is an independently managed compliance artifact — created when a license application is approved, updated on renewal or status change, and retired on expiry or revocation. This is the SSOT for employee-level gaming regulatory authorization across all jurisdictions.. Existence Justification: In Sports Entertainment\'s gaming compliance operations, specific employees (compliance officers, legal counsel, regulatory affairs staff) hold individual licenses or authorizations in multiple gaming jurisdictions simultaneously (e.g., NJ, PA, NV, CO), and each jurisdiction has multiple licensed employees operating within it. This is an actively managed operational relationship — the business must track which employee is licensed in which jurisdiction, under what role, with what license number, effective dates, and current status. This is not derivable from transactional data; it is a directly managed compliance record.' .

ind:VendorAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Partner ;
    rdfs:label 'Vendor Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Role-based assignment between an internal employee and an external vendor. It captures which employees are responsible for managing, liaising with, or overseeing a given vendor relationship, in what capacity, and for what period. Each record links one employee to one vendor with a defined role, scope, and tenure — attributes that exist only in the context of this assignment and cannot reside on either the employee or vendor master record alone.. Existence Justification: In sports-entertainment operations, employees actively manage vendor relationships across multiple domains — a procurement manager handles multiple broadcast technology vendors, a venue operations director manages multiple facility service providers, and a legal counsel oversees multiple contractor agreements simultaneously. Conversely, a single vendor (e.g., a broadcast technology partner) interacts with multiple internal employees across procurement, legal, finance, and operations departments. This is an operational \'Account Management Assignment\' concept that the business actively creates, updates, and terminates — it is not derivable from transactional data alone.' .

ind:VenueActivation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Venue Activation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Activation between a facility and a sponsorship deal. It captures the operational record of a specific sponsorship deal being activated at a specific facility, including the physical or digital placement details, asset type, activation zone, and the contracted value allocated to that facility-deal pairing. Each record links one facility to one deal and carries attributes that exist only in the context of this specific facility-deal relationship — enabling multi-venue deals and multi-deal facilities to be modeled accurately.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a single facility (e.g., a stadium) genuinely hosts multiple concurrent sponsorship deals simultaneously — naming rights, pouring rights, digital board placements, and presenting sponsorships all coexist at the same venue. Conversely, a single sponsorship deal can span multiple facilities — a regional pouring rights deal or a multi-venue naming rights package covers several arenas or stadiums under one commercial agreement. The business actively manages these facility-deal pairings as operational records with placement-specific attributes (activation zone, asset type, placement location, contracted value per facility) that belong to neither the facility nor the deal alone.' .

ind:Tenancy rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Tenancy' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Tenancy contract between a facility and a franchise. It captures the formal occupancy arrangement under which a franchise uses a specific venue asset — whether as a home stadium, practice facility, or training center — including the governing lease terms, revenue share obligations, and tenancy period. Each record links one facility to one franchise and carries attributes that exist only in the context of this specific occupancy relationship. Serves as the SSOT for all venue-franchise occupancy agreements consumed by venue operations, finance, and league governance.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a single facility (e.g., a shared stadium) genuinely hosts multiple franchise tenants simultaneously — an NFL team and an MLS team may both call the same venue home. Conversely, a franchise may operate across multiple facilities — a home stadium, a practice facility, and a training center — each governed by distinct lease or tenancy arrangements. The business actively manages these tenancy relationships with their own terms (start/end dates, tenancy type, revenue share percentage, lease agreement reference), making this a recognized operational concept called \'Tenancy\'.' .

ind:FacilityObligationApplicability rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Facility Obligation Applicability' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Compliance Applicability contract between a facility and a compliance obligation. It captures the operational record of which compliance obligations apply to which physical venues, including when applicability begins and ends, the current compliance status at that venue, who is responsible for maintaining compliance, and when it was last verified. Each record links one facility to one obligation and carries attributes that exist only in the context of that specific venue-obligation pairing — a single obligation may be compliant at one venue and in-remediation at another.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment operations, a physical venue (facility) is subject to multiple simultaneous compliance obligations — ADA Title III, OSHA safety standards, ISO 20121, local fire codes, and CBA venue requirements all apply concurrently to a single stadium. Conversely, a single obligation such as ADA Title III applies across every facility in the portfolio. The business actively manages this relationship through compliance programs that track per-facility obligation status, responsible owners, verification dates, and applicability windows — this is not derivable from transactional data but is an operationally managed compliance record.' .

ind:FranchiseDistributionRight rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Franchise Distribution Right' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between a franchise and a digital touchpoint governing the official distribution of that franchise\'s content and brand on a specific fan-facing digital channel. It captures the authorized rights tier, exclusivity terms, touchpoint role, and effective period for each franchise-channel pairing. Each record links one franchise to one digital touchpoint with attributes that exist only in the context of this distribution rights arrangement — managed by digital rights and DTC operations teams.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment DTC operations, a franchise (e.g., LA Lakers) is officially distributed across multiple digital touchpoints (team app, league OTT platform, web portal, venue kiosk), and each digital touchpoint hosts multiple franchises. This is not an analytical correlation — it is an actively managed distribution rights arrangement where the business must track which franchises are authorized on which channels, under what content rights tier, with what exclusivity terms, and for what effective period. Business stakeholders in digital distribution and rights management explicitly manage these pairings as \'franchise distribution agreements\' or \'channel distribution rights.\'' .

ind:RegulatoryOversight rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Regulatory Oversight' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the formal regulatory oversight relationship (Contract/Registration) between a franchise and a governing body. It captures the specific compliance obligations, registration standing, and jurisdictional scope that apply to each franchise-governing body pairing. Each record documents one governing body\'s authority over one franchise, including the type of oversight exercised, the franchise\'s registration or membership identifier with that body, current compliance status, and the effective dates of the oversight relationship. This is the system of record for franchise-level regulatory compliance tracking.. Existence Justification: A franchise is simultaneously subject to oversight from multiple governing bodies — the league office (NFL/NBA/etc.), anti-doping authorities (WADA), broadcast regulators (FCC), labor/safety bodies (OSHA/ADA), and potentially state athletic commissions — all at the same time. Conversely, each governing body (e.g., WADA, OSHA) oversees many franchises across the league. This is an active, operationally managed compliance relationship: franchises must register with each body, maintain compliance status per body, and track jurisdiction-specific obligations — none of which can be captured by a single FK on either entity.' .

ind:Accreditation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Compliance ;
    rdfs:label 'Accreditation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the formal Accreditation relationship between a governing_body and a vendor. It captures the operational record of a governing body certifying or recognizing a vendor as qualified to operate within a specific regulatory framework or compliance scope. Each record links one governing_body to one vendor and carries accreditation-specific attributes — status, scope, applicable framework, and verification dates — that exist only in the context of this pairing and cannot reside on either the vendor or governing body master record alone.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, governing bodies such as WADA, national anti-doping organizations, and league offices formally accredit or certify specific vendors (e.g., anti-doping labs, broadcast technology providers, medical suppliers) to operate within their regulatory frameworks. A single vendor can hold accreditations from multiple governing bodies simultaneously (e.g., a lab accredited by both WADA and a national anti-doping authority), and a single governing body accredits many vendors across its jurisdiction. This is an actively managed operational relationship — compliance teams create, renew, suspend, and audit these accreditations as a core business process.' .

ind:PresaleAccess rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Ticketing ;
    rdfs:label 'Presale Access' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Presale Access contract between a hold_allocation and a fan_segment. It captures the operational grant of access rights that a specific fan segment holds against a specific ticket inventory block, including the quantity allocated to that segment, its priority rank among competing segments, any segment-specific presale window overrides, and post-sale conversion performance. Each record links one hold_allocation to one fan_segment with attributes that exist only in the context of this per-segment access entitlement and cannot be stored on either parent entity.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment operations, a presale hold allocation is deliberately made accessible to multiple fan segments simultaneously — for example, a sponsor comp block may be opened to both \'Season Ticket Holders\' and \'Credit Card Partner Members\' with different priority ranks and quantities per segment. Conversely, a single fan segment (e.g., \'High-Value Loyalists\') can have access to multiple hold allocations across different events and hold types throughout a season. The business actively manages these per-segment access grants as operational records, tracking allocation quantities, priority ordering, presale window overrides, and post-sale conversion rates for each segment-allocation pairing.' .

ind:ChannelJurisdictionAuthorization rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Content ;
    rdfs:label 'Channel Jurisdiction Authorization' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the regulatory Authorization contract between a platform_channel and a gaming_jurisdiction. It captures the per-channel, per-jurisdiction compliance record that governs whether and how a distribution platform channel is permitted to deliver wagering-related content within a specific gaming regulatory jurisdiction. Each record links one platform_channel to one gaming_jurisdiction and carries the authorization status, effective dates, and regulatory approval reference that exist only in the context of this specific channel-jurisdiction pairing.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, a streaming or broadcast platform channel (e.g., an OTT app or DTC streaming service) must obtain regulatory authorization to operate in each gaming jurisdiction where it distributes wagering-related content. A single platform channel operates across many jurisdictions (e.g., a national OTT app active in 15 licensed US states), and each jurisdiction governs multiple platform channels (e.g., New Jersey authorizes ESPN+, FanDuel TV, and a DTC app). The business actively manages this relationship as a named compliance process — tracking per-jurisdiction authorization status, effective dates, and regulatory approval references for each platform-channel/jurisdiction combination.' .

ind:StreamingRightsAuthorization rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:League ;
    rdfs:label 'Streaming Rights Authorization' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between season and digital_touchpoint. It captures the formal authorization granting a specific digital touchpoint the right to distribute content from a specific league season under defined broadcast rights terms, geographic scope, and validity window. Each record links one season to one digital_touchpoint with attributes that exist only in the context of this rights grant — including the rights tier, streaming type, geo-restriction scope, and effective dates. This is the system of record for digital broadcast rights compliance across all fan-facing channels.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment, broadcast rights are actively managed contracts that authorize specific digital touchpoints (OTT app, mobile app, web portal) to stream content from specific seasons under defined rights tiers, geo-restrictions, and time windows. A single season\'s content is distributed across multiple authorized digital channels simultaneously, and each digital touchpoint carries content from multiple seasons (live current season plus archived past seasons). This relationship — a broadcast rights authorization — is a core compliance and rights management operation that the business actively creates, updates, and audits.' .

ind:SectionPricingAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Venue ;
    rdfs:label 'Section Pricing Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between seating_section and price_tier. It captures the operational pricing assignment that maps a specific seating section to a specific price tier for a defined effective period and event context. Each record links one seating_section to one price_tier with attributes — effective dates, face value override, and dynamic pricing flag — that exist only in the context of this section-tier assignment and cannot be stored on either entity alone.. Existence Justification: In sports entertainment venue operations, a seating section is assigned to multiple price tiers across different event types, seasons, and promotional windows (e.g., Section 101 is GA-priced for a concert but VIP-priced for a playoff game). Conversely, a single price tier (e.g., \'Club Level Premium\') applies to multiple seating sections simultaneously. The business actively manages these section-to-tier assignments with effective date ranges, face values, and dynamic pricing flags that belong to the assignment itself — not to either the section or the tier in isolation.' .

ind:PromotionSkuInclusion rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Merchandise ;
    rdfs:label 'Promotion Sku Inclusion' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Contract between sku_catalog and promotion. It captures the operational record of which specific SKUs are included in a promotional campaign and under what per-SKU terms. Each record links one SKU to one promotion and carries attributes — discount overrides, channel restrictions, and effective date windows — that exist only in the context of this specific SKU-promotion pairing and cannot be stored on either the SKU catalog or the promotion campaign alone.. Existence Justification: In sports merchandise retail, promotions are explicitly multi-SKU campaigns (e.g., \'all championship gear 30% off\', \'BOGO on team jerseys\') where a single promotion applies to many SKUs simultaneously, and a single SKU participates in multiple promotions across a season (e.g., a jersey SKU is included in a championship launch promo, a fan loyalty redemption promo, and an event-day discount promo). The current model stores applicable_sku_list as a denormalized STRING on the promotion record, which is a textbook normalization deficiency signaling an unmodeled M:N. The business actively manages which specific SKUs are included in each promotion, with per-SKU discount overrides, channel restrictions, and effective date windows that belong to the inclusion record itself — not to either the SKU catalog or the promotion campaign.' .

